<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_title">On the power of (approximate) reward models for inference-time scaling</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><span class="ltx_text ltx_bib_journal">arXiv preprint arXiv:2602.01381</span>.
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited">Cited by: <a href="#S1.SS1.p2.1" title="1.1 Setting: Guided Generation with Imperfect Process Rewards ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§1.1</span></a>,
<a href="#S3.SS1.p6.1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§3.1</span></a>.
</span></li>
</ul>
</section>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:298%;">Contents of Appendix</span></p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Comparison with Prior Work</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we discuss how our theoretical guarantees compare with prior work. We specify to the autoregressive generation setting, as the more general setting has not been theoretically studied in the past.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Action-level rejection sampling / sequential importance sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang and Klein, 2021</a>)</cite></h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This algorithm samples <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:H}</annotation></semantics></math> autoregressively via the conditional distributions</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\pi}(a_{h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\propto\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{1:h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h+1})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}(a_{h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\propto\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{1:h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It can be implemented in expected time <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(H\widehat{C}_{\mathsf{act}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(H\widehat{C}_{\mathsf{act}})</annotation></semantics></math> by rejection sampling / importance sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite>, and by <a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2 Preliminaries ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, it exactly samples from <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}=V^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}=V^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, even under assumption <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> with <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{C}_{\infty}=1+\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{C}_{\infty}=1+\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, it can incur <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\epsilon\sqrt{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>H</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\epsilon\sqrt{H})</annotation></semantics></math> sampling error <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite>, which is vacuous if e.g. <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=\Theta(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">VGB <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al., 2025</a>)</cite></h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This algorithm is defined by a random walk on the <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">tree of autoregressive generations</em>, which has state space <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{0}\sqcup\dots\sqcup\mathcal{A}^{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>⊔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊔</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{0}\sqcup\dots\sqcup\mathcal{A}^{H}</annotation></semantics></math> and in which the parent of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The first main result of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite> is that the random walk samples from <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, up to total variation error <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, in time roughly <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(H^{2}C_{\sf act}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}\log(1/\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(H^{2}C_{\sf act}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}\log(1/\delta))</annotation></semantics></math>. This guarantee is essentially matched by the guarantee of <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Beyond SMC: Faster Convergence under 𝐿_∞-condition ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> for SMC, except the language model evaluations in SMC can be parallelized into <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> rounds, whereas the language model evaluations in VGB are inherently sequential.<span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            The results of <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> suggest a potential approach to parallelizing VGB via particle filtering, but it is unclear in what generality such a simulation would be efficient.</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The second main result of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite> shows that under the following average-case closeness condition between <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as bounded action-level coverage, VGB samples from a distribution that <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">approximately covers</em> <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{assumption}</span>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">[Average-case assumption of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite>]</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max\left\{\En^{\pi^{\star}}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}{V^{\star}(a_{1:h})}\right],\En^{\pi^{\star}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(a_{1:h})}{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}\right]\right\}\leq C." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\left\{\En^{\pi^{\star}}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}{V^{\star}(a_{1:h})}\right],\En^{\pi^{\star}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(a_{1:h})}{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}\right]\right\}\leq C.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We make the following observation:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{fact}</span>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq h\leq H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq h\leq H</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)=\En^{\pi^{\star}}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}{V^{\star}(a_{1:h})}\right]\cdot\En^{\pi^{\star}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(a_{1:h})}{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}\right]-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)=\En^{\pi^{\star}}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}{V^{\star}(a_{1:h})}\right]\cdot\En^{\pi^{\star}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(a_{1:h})}{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}\right]-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, under <a href="#A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="VGB ( , ) ‣ Appendix A Comparison with Prior Work ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> as well as bounded action-level coverage, <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> shows that SMC with <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leq(C+1)^{2}H^{2}/\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leq(C+1)^{2}H^{2}/\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> particles samples from a distribution that is <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-close in total variation distance to <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that closeness in total variation distance is a stronger guarantee than approximate coverage.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Technical Tools</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{proposition}</span>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, independent random variables <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\cdots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\cdots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left\lvert\sum_{i=1}^{n}(X_{i}-\En[X_{i}])\right\rvert\leq\sqrt{nR\max_{i}\En\lvert X_{i}\rvert}+2n\max_{i}\En\left[\lvert X_{i}\rvert\mathbb{I}\{\lvert X_{i}\rvert\geq R\}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>nR</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left\lvert\sum_{i=1}^{n}(X_{i}-\En[X_{i}])\right\rvert\leq\sqrt{nR\max_{i}\En\lvert X_{i}\rvert}+2n\max_{i}\En\left[\lvert X_{i}\rvert\mathbb{I}\{\lvert X_{i}\rvert\geq R\}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We define <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}=\min\{\max\{X_{i},-R\},R\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}=\min\{\max\{X_{i},-R\},R\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}=X_{i}-Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}=X_{i}-Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can bound</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left\lvert\sum_{i=1}^{n}(X_{i}-\En[X_{i}])\right\rvert\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left\lvert\sum_{i=1}^{n}(X_{i}-\En[X_{i}])\right\rvert\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\En\left\lvert\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Y_{i}-\En[Y_{i}])\right\rvert+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\En\lvert Z_{i}-\En[Z_{i}]\rvert." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En\left\lvert\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Y_{i}-\En[Y_{i}])\right\rvert+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\En\lvert Z_{i}-\En[Z_{i}]\rvert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\En\lvert Z_{i}-\En[Z_{i}]\rvert\leq 2\En\lvert Z_{i}\rvert\leq 2\En\left[\lvert X_{i}\rvert\mathbb{I}\{\lvert X_{i}\rvert\geq R\}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En\lvert Z_{i}-\En[Z_{i}]\rvert\leq 2\En\lvert Z_{i}\rvert\leq 2\En\left[\lvert X_{i}\rvert\mathbb{I}\{\lvert X_{i}\rvert\geq R\}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. Further,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\En\left\lvert\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Y_{i}-\En[Y_{i}])\right\rvert\right)^{2}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\En\left\lvert\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Y_{i}-\En[Y_{i}])\right\rvert\right)^{2}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\En\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Y_{i}-\En[Y_{i}])\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Y_{i}-\En[Y_{i}])\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\En(Y_{i}-\En[Y_{i}])^{2}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{n}\En Y_{i}^{2}\leq R\sum_{i=1}^{n}\En\lvert X_{i}\rvert," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\En(Y_{i}-\En[Y_{i}])^{2}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{n}\En Y_{i}^{2}\leq R\sum_{i=1}^{n}\En\lvert X_{i}\rvert,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where we use <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lvert Y_{i}\rvert\leq\min\{\lvert X_{i}\rvert,R\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lvert Y_{i}\rvert\leq\min\{\lvert X_{i}\rvert,R\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof is then completed by combining the inequalities above.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs for SMC</h2>

<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h}=\{(\tilde{x}_{\ell}^{i},x_{\ell}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\}_{\ell\in[h],i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h}=\{(\tilde{x}_{\ell}^{i},x_{\ell}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\}_{\ell\in[h],i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the full history of the execution of SMC (<a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) up to the end of iteration <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. We write <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En_{h}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En_{h}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> for the conditional distribution with respect to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. We write <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z:=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:H}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[r^{\star}(x_{H})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z:=\mathbb{E}_{x_{1:H}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[r^{\star}(x_{H})]</annotation></semantics></math> and observe that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\pi_{h}}[V^{\star}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\pi_{h}}[V^{\star}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Useful Lemmas for SMC</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first prove the following lemmas.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For any step <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> and any function <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathcal{X}_{h}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathcal{X}_{h}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g\right]\right]=\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\frac{\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h})\cdot g(x_{h})\right]}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g\right]\right]=\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\frac{\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h})\cdot g(x_{h})\right]}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The next lemma follows from applying <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> inductively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{h}:\mathcal{X}_{h}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{h}:\mathcal{X}_{h}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{h}}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{h}}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">In particular, <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]=\widehat{Z}_{h}=\En[\widehat{V}(x_{h})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]=\widehat{Z}_{h}=\En[\widehat{V}(x_{h})]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{H}\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]=Z\cdot\pi^{\star}_{H}(x),\qquad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{H}\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]=Z\cdot\pi^{\star}_{H}(x),\qquad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we upper bound the TV error of <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> by the deviation of <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{W}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{W}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
For <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq\frac{1}{2Z}\En\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\rvert." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq\frac{1}{2Z}\En\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\rvert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> and <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>. </span>
To prove <a href="#A3.E18" title="In C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, observe that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\En_{h-1}\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}g(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\En_{h-1}\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}g(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\En_{h-1}\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}g(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\En_{h-1}\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}g(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. given <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, for each <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}g(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{x}_{h-1}\sim\hat{\nu}_{h-1}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid\tilde{x}_{h-1})}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1})}g(x_{h})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}g(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{x}_{h-1}\sim\hat{\nu}_{h-1}}\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid\tilde{x}_{h-1})}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1})}g(x_{h})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">which establishes <a href="#A3.E18" title="In C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>. Next, we argue that <a href="#A3.E19" title="In C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> holds inductively (noting that the base case is trivial since <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{W}_{0}=\widehat{V}(\perp)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{W}_{0}=\widehat{V}(\perp)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\nu}_{0}=\delta_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\nu}_{0}=\delta_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>), using <a href="#A3.E18" title="In C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\widehat{\nu}_{H}}[g_{h}]\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{\widehat{\nu}_{H}}[g_{h}]\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h})\cdot g_{h}(x_{h})\right]}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h})\cdot g_{h}(x_{h})\right]}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})\cdot\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}[\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})]}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})\cdot\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}[\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})]}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p">as desired. We get that <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{W}_{h}]=\mathbb{E}[\widehat{V}(x_{h})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{W}_{h}]=\mathbb{E}[\widehat{V}(x_{h})]</annotation></semantics></math> by using <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{h}\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{h}\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, <a href="#A3.E20" title="In C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> follows by setting <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{H}(x)=\mathbb{I}\{x_{H}=x\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{H}(x)=\mathbb{I}\{x_{H}=x\}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A3.E19" title="In C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> and using that <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}(x_{H})=V^{\star}(x_{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}(x_{H})=V^{\star}(x_{H})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{H}\in\mathcal{X}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{H}\in\mathcal{X}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>. </span>
By <a href="#A3.E20" title="In C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, we can write</p>
<table id="A3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2ZD_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2ZD_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}}\lvert Z\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)]-Z\pi^{\star}_{H}(x)\rvert=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}}\left\lvert Z\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)]-\En[\widehat{W}_{H}\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)]\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}}\lvert Z\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)]-Z\pi^{\star}_{H}(x)\rvert=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}}\left\lvert Z\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)]-\En[\widehat{W}_{H}\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)]\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}}\En\left[\left\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\right\rvert\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]=\En\left[\left\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\right\rvert\cdot\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}}\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]=\En\left\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\right\rvert." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}}\En\left[\left\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\right\rvert\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]=\En\left[\left\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\right\rvert\cdot\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}}\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]=\En\left\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\right\rvert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove a slightly stronger upper bound.
<span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{proposition}</span>
SMC (<a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) with <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> particles achieves</p>
<table id="A3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sqrt{\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})]\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sqrt{\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})]\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> then follows from the fact that <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\star}(x_{h})\leq C_{\sf act}V^{\star}(x_{h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\star}(x_{h})\leq C_{\sf act}V^{\star}(x_{h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely under <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid{}x_{h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid{}x_{h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A3.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})]\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]=1+D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h-1}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h-1}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})]\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]=1+D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h-1}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>. </span>
We define <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(x)=\frac{V^{\star}(x)}{\widehat{V}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(x)=\frac{V^{\star}(x)}{\widehat{V}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A3.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{h}=\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{h}=\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then <a href="#A3.E18" title="In C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> with <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=\rho(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=\rho(x)</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale with <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0}=Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0}=Z</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{H}=\widehat{W}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{H}=\widehat{W}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can then decompose</p>
<table id="A3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\rvert\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\rvert\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Next, we note that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{M_{h}-M_{h-1}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{M_{h}-M_{h-1}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widehat{W}_{h-1}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\rho(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})-\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widehat{W}_{h-1}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\rho(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})-\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widehat{W}_{h-1}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widehat{W}_{h-1}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Since the tuples <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. given <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can bound</p>
<table id="A3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\widehat{W}_{h-1}^{2}}\En_{h-1}(M_{h}-M_{h-1})^{2}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\widehat{W}_{h-1}^{2}}\En_{h-1}(M_{h}-M_{h-1})^{2}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E37.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\mathrm{Var}_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid{}x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\mathrm{Var}_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid{}x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\frac{\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}[V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}]}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})^{2}}\right]=\vcentcolon\Delta_{h-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\frac{\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}[V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}]}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})^{2}}\right]=\vcentcolon\Delta_{h-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Then, by <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}]\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\Delta_{h-1}]=\frac{1}{N}\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})]\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}]\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\Delta_{h-1}]=\frac{1}{N}\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})]\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we can bound</p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\rvert\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\rvert\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{h=1}^{H}\En\left[\En_{h-1}\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{h=1}^{H}\En\left[\En_{h-1}\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{h=1}^{H}\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\sqrt{\Delta_{h-1}}\right]\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sqrt{\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}]\cdot\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\Delta_{h-1}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{h=1}^{H}\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\sqrt{\Delta_{h-1}}\right]\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sqrt{\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}]\cdot\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\Delta_{h-1}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sqrt{\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})]\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sqrt{\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})]\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Combining the inequalities above completes the proof.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Insufficiency of Existing Analysis</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Most non-asymptotic analyses of SMC assume conditions at least as strong as the <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> closeness in <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Del Moral, 2004</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cérou et al., 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Whiteley et al., 2012</a>)</cite>. Another line of work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Marion and Schmidler, 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee and Santana-Gijzen, 2024</a>)</cite> imposes assumptions on the transition kernel, which are therefore incomparable to those in this paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We note that these approaches might fail to capture SMC convergence when we assume only <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-closeness (<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>). This is because many explicitly or implicitly control the variance <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h}))_{h\in[H]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h}))_{h\in[H]}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cérou et al., 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Whiteley et al., 2012</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schweizer, 2012</a>, etc.)</cite>. In contrast, our proof of <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> proceeds via the absolute deviation <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En\lvert M_{H}-Z\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En\lvert M_{H}-Z\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>. The seemingly more natural attempt to study the variance <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En(M_{H}-Z)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En(M_{H}-Z)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> must confront the fact that <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{H}=\widehat{W}_{H}=\prod_{h=1}^{H}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{H}=\widehat{W}_{H}=\prod_{h=1}^{H}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequential product. As the following lemma suggests, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> need not be controlled when the <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> divergences <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right))_{h\in[H]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right))_{h\in[H]}</annotation></semantics></math> are bounded.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Suppose that <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}(\perp)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}(\perp)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h})=\En(\widehat{W}_{h}-\widehat{Z}_{h})^{2}\geq\frac{\mathrm{Var}_{x_{1}\sim\pi_{1}}(\En[\widehat{V}(x_{h})\mid x_{1}])}{N}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h})=\En(\widehat{W}_{h}-\widehat{Z}_{h})^{2}\geq\frac{\mathrm{Var}_{x_{1}\sim\pi_{1}}(\En[\widehat{V}(x_{h})\mid x_{1}])}{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">In particular, for <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a problem instance <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V^{\star},\widehat{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V^{\star},\widehat{V})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and both <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> holds with <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sf act}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sf act}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, but SMC with <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> particles incurs</p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{h\in[H]}\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h})\geq\frac{2^{\lfloor H/2\rfloor}-2}{N}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{h\in[H]}\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h})\geq\frac{2^{\lfloor H/2\rfloor}-2}{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, if convergence of SMC is established via upper bounds on <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>, the rate can be vacuous unless we have <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq\exp(\Omega(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq\exp(\Omega(H))</annotation></semantics></math> particles. For example,
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schweizer (2012)</a></cite> study SMC through the following relation (cf. Lemma 2.1 therein) for <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathcal{X}_{H}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathcal{X}_{H}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left(\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{H}}[f]-\En_{\pi^{\star}_{H}}[f]\right)^{2}\leq 2\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{H}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{H}}[f])+2\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{H})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left(\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{H}}[f]-\En_{\pi^{\star}_{H}}[f]\right)^{2}\leq 2\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{H}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{H}}[f])+2\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{H}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Consequently, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schweizer (2012)</a></cite> establish upper bounds of the form</p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N\cdot\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{H}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{H}}[f])\leq C_{0}(f)+C_{1}(f)\cdot\epsilon_{N}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N\cdot\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{H}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{H}}[f])\leq C_{0}(f)+C_{1}(f)\cdot\epsilon_{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0},C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0},C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are two problem-dependent functionals, and <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined so that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\epsilon_{N}\geq\max_{h\in[H]}\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\epsilon_{N}\geq\max_{h\in[H]}\mathrm{Var}(\widehat{W}_{h}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">This implies that the analysis in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schweizer (2012)</a></cite> cannot recover the upper bound of <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> (and <a href="#S3.SS1.SSS1" title="3.1.1 Handling Tail Behavior ‣ 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Insufficiency of Existing Analysis ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>. </span>
For any <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leq\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leq\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{\ell}(x_{h})=\En[\widehat{V}(x_{\ell})\mid{}x_{h}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{\ell}(x_{h})=\En[\widehat{V}(x_{\ell})\mid{}x_{h}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\ell}(x_{h})=\frac{\widetilde{V}_{\ell}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\ell}(x_{h})=\frac{\widetilde{V}_{\ell}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we define <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{h,\ell}=\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho_{\ell}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{h,\ell}=\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho_{\ell}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it is straightforward to verify that <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{h,\ell})_{h\in[\ell]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{h,\ell})_{h\in[\ell]}</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale with <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0,\ell}=\widehat{Z}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0,\ell}=\widehat{Z}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\ell,\ell}=\widehat{W}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\ell,\ell}=\widehat{W}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we can lower bound</p>
<table id="A3.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En(\widehat{W}_{\ell}-\widehat{Z}_{\ell})^{2}\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En(\widehat{W}_{\ell}-\widehat{Z}_{\ell})^{2}\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\En(M_{1,\ell}-\widehat{Z}_{\ell})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En(M_{1,\ell}-\widehat{Z}_{\ell})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\En\left[\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\widetilde{V}_{\ell}(x_{1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{0}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{0}}[\rho_{\ell}]\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En\left[\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\widetilde{V}_{\ell}(x_{1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{0}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{0}}[\rho_{\ell}]\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\left(\En_{x_{1}\sim\pi_{1}}[\widetilde{V}_{\ell}(x_{1})^{2}]-\widehat{Z}_{\ell}^{2}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\left(\En_{x_{1}\sim\pi_{1}}[\widetilde{V}_{\ell}(x_{1})^{2}]-\widehat{Z}_{\ell}^{2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where we note that <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}_{0}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">⟂</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}_{0}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=\perp</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Now, consider <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\lfloor H/2\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\lfloor H/2\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the following simple example:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{h}=\{(h,0),(h,1)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{h}=\{(h,0),(h,1)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P((h+1,i)\mid(h,i))=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P((h+1,i)\mid(h,i))=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The initial distribution is given by <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}((1,0))=\frac{1}{2^{n}}=\pi_{1}((1,1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}((1,0))=\frac{1}{2^{n}}=\pi_{1}((1,1))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reward function is <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\star}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\star}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, we set <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}((h,1))=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}((h,1))=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}((h,0))=2^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}((h,0))=2^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}((h,0))=2^{(2n-h)_{+}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}((h,0))=2^{(2n-h)_{+}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\geq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\geq n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Then, it is clear that both <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> hold with <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sf act}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sf act}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}((h,0))=\frac{p\widehat{V}((h,0))}{p\widehat{V}((h,0))+1-p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}((h,0))=\frac{p\widehat{V}((h,0))}{p\widehat{V}((h,0))+1-p}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}((h,0))\in[p,\frac{1}{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>,</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}((h,0))\in[p,\frac{1}{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. This immediately implies <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">However, we can then calculate <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}_{n}((1,0))=2^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}_{n}((1,0))=2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En[\widetilde{V}_{n}(x_{1})^{2}]\geq p\cdot 2^{2n}=2^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En[\widetilde{V}_{n}(x_{1})^{2}]\geq p\cdot 2^{2n}=2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives the desired statement.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.SS1.SSS1" title="3.1.1 Handling Tail Behavior ‣ 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the following general version of <a href="#S3.SS1.SSS1" title="3.1.1 Handling Tail Behavior ‣ 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1.1</span></a>.
<span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{theorem}</span>

SMC with <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> particles achieves the following for any <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq H\sqrt{\frac{M\eta}{N}}+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left[\mathrm{Cov}_{M}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)+\mathrm{Cov}_{\eta,h}^{\mathsf{act}}\left(\pi^{\star}\,\|\,\pi_{\texttt{ref}}\right)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq H\sqrt{\frac{M\eta}{N}}+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left[\mathrm{Cov}_{M}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)+\mathrm{Cov}_{\eta,h}^{\mathsf{act}}\left(\pi^{\star}\,\|\,\pi_{\texttt{ref}}\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we define</p>
<table id="A3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{\eta,h}^{\mathsf{act}}\left(\pi^{\star}\,\|\,\pi_{\texttt{ref}}\right)\vcentcolon=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{\eta,h}^{\mathsf{act}}\left(\pi^{\star}\,\|\,\pi_{\texttt{ref}}\right)\vcentcolon=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E52.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left(\frac{\pi^{\star}(x_{h}\mid x_{h-1})}{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(x_{h}\mid x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left(\frac{\pi^{\star}(x_{h}\mid x_{h-1})}{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(x_{h}\mid x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E53.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The quantity <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}_{\eta,h}^{\mathsf{act}}\left(\pi^{\star}\,\|\,\pi_{\texttt{ref}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}_{\eta,h}^{\mathsf{act}}\left(\pi^{\star}\,\|\,\pi_{\texttt{ref}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is the action-level analogue of <a href="#S3.SS1.SSS1" title="3.1.1 Handling Tail Behavior ‣ 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1.1</span></a>.
Under <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, this additional term is <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\geq C_{\sf act}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\geq C_{\sf act}</annotation></semantics></math>, recovering <a href="#S3.SS1.SSS1" title="3.1.1 Handling Tail Behavior ‣ 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We follow the notation of the proof of <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> (<a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>). Recall that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{M_{h}-M_{h-1}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{M_{h}-M_{h-1}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widehat{W}_{h-1}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widehat{W}_{h-1}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the tuples <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. given <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Technical Tools ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, for any fixed parameter <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we can bound</p>
<table id="A3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{\widehat{W}_{h-1}}\En_{h-1}\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{\widehat{W}_{h-1}}\En_{h-1}\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\frac{R}{N}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]}+2\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq R\right\}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\frac{R}{N}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]}+2\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq R\right\}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">By <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\sqrt{\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]}\right]\leq\sqrt{\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}]\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]]}\leq\sqrt{\widehat{Z}_{h-1}\cdot Z}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\sqrt{\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]}\right]\leq\sqrt{\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}]\En[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]]}\leq\sqrt{\widehat{Z}_{h-1}\cdot Z},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">and similarly, for any <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq R\right\}\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h-1}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq R\right\}\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E60.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[V^{\star}(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq R\right\}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[V^{\star}(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq R\right\}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E61.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[V^{\star}(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta^{-1}R\right\}+V^{\star}(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right\}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>R</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[V^{\star}(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta^{-1}R\right\}+V^{\star}(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\left\{\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right\}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E62.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~Z\cdot\left[\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1}}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta^{-1}R\right)+\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~Z\cdot\left[\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1}}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta^{-1}R\right)+\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">where we use <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h-1}(x_{h-1})\cdot V^{\star}(x_{h-1})=\pi^{\star}_{h-1}(x_{h-1})\cdot Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h-1}(x_{h-1})\cdot V^{\star}(x_{h-1})=\pi^{\star}_{h-1}(x_{h-1})\cdot Z</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h-1}\in\mathcal{X}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h-1}\in\mathcal{X}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(x_{h}\mid{}x_{h-1})\cdot V^{\star}(x_{h})=\pi^{\star}(x_{h}\mid{}x_{h-1})\cdot Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(x_{h}\mid{}x_{h-1})\cdot V^{\star}(x_{h})=\pi^{\star}(x_{h}\mid{}x_{h-1})\cdot Z</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, we can choose <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=M\eta\frac{Z}{\widehat{Z}_{h-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=M\eta\frac{Z}{\widehat{Z}_{h-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> to derive</p>
<table id="A3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{Z}\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{Z}\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\frac{M\eta}{N}}+2\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1}}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq M\cdot\frac{Z}{\widehat{Z}_{h-1}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\frac{M\eta}{N}}+2\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1}}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\geq M\cdot\frac{Z}{\widehat{Z}_{h-1}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~+2\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~+2\mathbb{P}_{x_{h-1}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left(\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})}{V^{\star}(x_{h-1})}\geq\eta\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Taking summation completes the proof.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Beyond SMC: Faster Convergence under 𝐿_∞-condition ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first prove the following lemma.
<span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>

Under <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, for any <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if we run SMC (<a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) with <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\Omega(H\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2}\log(H/\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\Omega(H\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2}\log(H/\delta))</annotation></semantics></math> particles, then with probability at least <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|\leq Z/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|\leq Z/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We follow the notation of the proof of <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> (<a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>). Recall that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{M_{h}-M_{h-1}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{M_{h}-M_{h-1}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widehat{W}_{h-1}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widehat{W}_{h-1}\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the tuples <math id="A3.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. given <math id="A3.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that by <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, it holds that almost surely</p>
<table id="A3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}=\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{V^{\star}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}\cdot\frac{V^{\star}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}\leq C_{\sf act}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}=\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{V^{\star}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}\cdot\frac{V^{\star}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}\leq C_{\sf act}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using the fact that for a random variable <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in[0,A]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in[0,A]</annotation></semantics></math>, we can bound <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[e^{\lambda(Y-\mathbb{E}[Y])}]\leq e^{\lambda^{2}A^{2}/8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[e^{\lambda(Y-\mathbb{E}[Y])}]\leq e^{\lambda^{2}A^{2}/8}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that for any <math id="A3.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}[\exp(\lambda(M_{h}-M_{h-1}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}[\exp(\lambda(M_{h}-M_{h-1}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}\left[\exp\left(\lambda\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\mathbb{E}_{\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}\left[\exp\left(\lambda\widehat{W}_{h-1}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}{\widehat{V}(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})}-\mathbb{E}_{\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}[\rho(x_{h-1})]\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\exp\left(\frac{1}{N}\lambda^{2}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}C_{\sf act}^{2}\widehat{W}_{h-1}^{2}\right)}\leq{\exp\left(\frac{1}{N}\lambda^{2}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2}M_{h-1}^{2}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\exp\left(\frac{1}{N}\lambda^{2}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}C_{\sf act}^{2}\widehat{W}_{h-1}^{2}\right)}\leq{\exp\left(\frac{1}{N}\lambda^{2}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2}M_{h-1}^{2}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By Freedman’s inequality, for any <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that with probability <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</p>
<table id="A3.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|M_{h}-Z|\leq\sum_{i=1}^{h-1}\frac{\lambda\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2}M_{i}^{2}}{N}+\frac{\log(2/\delta)}{\lambda}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|M_{h}-Z|\leq\sum_{i=1}^{h-1}\frac{\lambda\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2}M_{i}^{2}}{N}+\frac{\log(2/\delta)}{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Choosing <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=4\log(2H/\delta)/Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=4\log(2H/\delta)/Z</annotation></semantics></math> and using the union bound, it follows that with probability <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|M_{h}-Z|\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|M_{h}-Z|\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{4\log(2/\delta)\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2}}{N}\sum_{i=0}^{h-1}\frac{M_{i}^{2}}{Z}+\frac{Z}{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{4\log(2/\delta)\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2}}{N}\sum_{i=0}^{h-1}\frac{M_{i}^{2}}{Z}+\frac{Z}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Since we have chosen <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\Omega(H\log(H/\delta)\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\Omega(H\log(H/\delta)\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{4}C_{\sf act}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows from induction on <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> that in the event that <a href="#A3.E71" title="In C.5 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a> holds, we have that <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M_{h}-Z|\leq Z/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M_{h}-Z|\leq Z/2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, this implies that <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|\leq Z/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|\leq Z/2</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Beyond SMC: Faster Convergence under 𝐿_∞-condition ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. </span>
In any given round, let <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{p}</annotation></semantics></math> be the distribution of the output of <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with Option 2 (when <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> restarts we regard it as outputing the symbol “restart”). Then, the probability that the algorithm outputs any <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="A3.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{p}(x):=\mathbb{E}\left[\min\left\{1,\frac{\widehat{W}_{H}}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}\right\}\cdot\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]\leq\frac{Z\cdot\pi^{\star}_{H}(x)}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{p}(x):=\mathbb{E}\left[\min\left\{1,\frac{\widehat{W}_{H}}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}\right\}\cdot\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]\leq\frac{Z\cdot\pi^{\star}_{H}(x)}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where we have used <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.
Moreover, using that <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}\geq 2Z\geq\widehat{W}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}\geq 2Z\geq\widehat{W}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{\delta}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{\delta}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#A3.SS5" title="C.5 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>, for any subset <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathcal{X}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathcal{X}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{p}(X)=\mathbb{E}\left[\min\left\{1,\frac{\widehat{W}_{H}}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}\right\}\cdot\widehat{\nu}_{H}(X)\right]\geq\frac{Z\cdot\pi^{\star}_{H}(x)}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}-\frac{\delta}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{p}(X)=\mathbb{E}\left[\min\left\{1,\frac{\widehat{W}_{H}}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}\right\}\cdot\widehat{\nu}_{H}(X)\right]\geq\frac{Z\cdot\pi^{\star}_{H}(x)}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}-\frac{\delta}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p5.3" class="ltx_p">In particular, it holds that <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{Z}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}-\frac{\delta}{4\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}}\leq\widehat{p}(x\neq\text{restart})\leq\frac{Z}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mtext>restart</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{Z}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}-\frac{\delta}{4\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}}\leq\widehat{p}(x\neq\text{restart})\leq\frac{Z}{2\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence using <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Z}_{1}/Z\leq\mathsf{C}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Z}_{1}/Z\leq\mathsf{C}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that for any <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset\mathcal{X}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset\mathcal{X}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A3.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{\star}_{H}(X)-\delta\leq\widehat{p}(X\mid{}\text{not restart})\leq(1+\delta)\pi^{\star}_{H}(X)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mtext>not restart</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{\star}_{H}(X)-\delta\leq\widehat{p}(X\mid{}\text{not restart})\leq(1+\delta)\pi^{\star}_{H}(X),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p5.4" class="ltx_p">and hence <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{H},\widehat{p}(\cdot\mid{}\text{not restart})\right)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mtext>not restart</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{H},\widehat{p}(\cdot\mid{}\text{not restart})\right)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, using the guarantee of rejection sampling, we know the number of outer loop steps is bounded by <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\log(1/\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\log(1/\delta))</annotation></semantics></math>
by noting that <math id="A3.SS5.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Z}_{1}/Z\leq\mathsf{C}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Z}_{1}/Z\leq\mathsf{C}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6 </span>Lower Bound for SMC with Exact Value Function</h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the following proposition, we show that the horizon dependence of SMC when <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}=V^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}=V^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is not an artifact of our analysis.
<span id="A3.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{proposition}</span>
There exists a problem instance where <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}=V^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}=V^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> holds with <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sf act}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sf act}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, however SMC with <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> particles must incur</p>
<table id="A3.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\geq c\min\left\{1,\frac{\sqrt{H}}{N}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>H</mi></msqrt><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\geq c\min\left\{1,\frac{\sqrt{H}}{N}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We construct a problem instance as follows. Fix <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{h}=\{0,1\}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{h}=\{0,1\}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the transition kernel <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and value function <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}=V^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}=V^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid{}x)=\mathrm{unif}(\{(x,0),(x,1)\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>unif</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid{}x)=\mathrm{unif}(\{(x,0),(x,1)\})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}=V^{\star}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}=V^{\star}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined recursively as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\star}(\perp)=0,\qquad V^{\star}(x,0)=V^{\star}(x),\quad V^{\star}(x,1)=(1+\lambda)V^{\star}(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\star}(\perp)=0,\qquad V^{\star}(x,0)=V^{\star}(x),\quad V^{\star}(x,1)=(1+\lambda)V^{\star}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Then, it holds that <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sf act}\leq 1+\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sf act}\leq 1+\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}_{H}=\mathrm{Ber}\left(p\right)^{\otimes H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Ber</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}_{H}=\mathrm{Ber}\left(p\right)^{\otimes H}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\frac{1+\lambda}{2+\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\frac{1+\lambda}{2+\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Under this construction, we can rewrite SMC as follows (where <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\nu}_{0}=\delta_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\nu}_{0}=\delta_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
<ul id="A3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, sample <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> particles <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}},\ldots,\tilde{x}_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}(\cdot{})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}},\ldots,\tilde{x}_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}\overset{\text{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}(\cdot{})</annotation></semantics></math> and generates <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\sim\mathrm{unif}(\{0,1\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\sim\mathrm{unif}(\{0,1\})</annotation></semantics></math> independently.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assign weights <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=1+\lambda a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=1+\lambda a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}</annotation></semantics></math> to particle <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=(\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}},a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define weighted empirical measure <math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\nu}_{h}\vcentcolon={}\frac{1}{W_{h}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\updelta_{x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\nu}_{h}\vcentcolon={}\frac{1}{W_{h}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\updelta_{x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{h}=N+\lambda\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{h}=N+\lambda\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We make the following claims, proven below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A3.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{claim}</span>
<p id="A3.SS6.p4.2" class="ltx_p">It holds that <math id="A3.SS6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}]=\mathrm{Ber}(p_{N})^{\otimes H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Ber</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}]=\mathrm{Ber}(p_{N})^{\otimes H}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#A3.E81" title="In C.6 Lower Bound for SMC with Exact Value Function ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A3.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{claim}</span>
<p id="A3.SS6.p5.2" class="ltx_p">It holds that <math id="A3.SS6.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{N}\leq\frac{1+\lambda}{2+\lambda}-\frac{c_{\lambda}}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{N}\leq\frac{1+\lambda}{2+\lambda}-\frac{c_{\lambda}}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS6.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\lambda}=\frac{2\lambda(1+\lambda)}{(2+\lambda)^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\lambda}=\frac{2\lambda(1+\lambda)}{(2+\lambda)^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we can lower bound</p>
<table id="A3.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)=D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\Bin(H,p),\Bin(H,p_{N})\right)\geq c\min\{1,\sqrt{H}\lvert p-p_{N}\rvert\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>H</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)=D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\Bin(H,p),\Bin(H,p_{N})\right)\geq c\min\{1,\sqrt{H}\lvert p-p_{N}\rvert\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is an absolute constant. Choosing <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof of <a href="#A3.SS6" title="C.6 Lower Bound for SMC with Exact Value Function ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the auxiliary claims:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A3.SS6" title="C.6 Lower Bound for SMC with Exact Value Function ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>. </span>
By definition, for any <math id="A3.SS6.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\nu}_{h}(x,1)=\frac{1}{W_{h}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\mathbb{I}\{\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=x,a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=a\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\nu}_{h}(x,1)=\frac{1}{W_{h}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\mathbb{I}\{\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=x,a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=a\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A3.SS6.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent, we can calculate</p>
<table id="A3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En[\widehat{\nu}_{h}(x,1)]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En[\widehat{\nu}_{h}(x,1)]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E79.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\En\left[\frac{1}{W_{h}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\mathbb{I}\{a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=1\}\cdot\mathbb{I}\{\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=x\}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En\left[\frac{1}{W_{h}}\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\mathbb{I}\{a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=1\}\cdot\mathbb{I}\{\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}=x\}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\En\left[\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}(x)\cdot\frac{(1+\lambda)\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}}{N+\lambda\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En\left[\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}(x)\cdot\frac{(1+\lambda)\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}}{N+\lambda\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A3.SS6.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{h}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\sim\Bin(N,\frac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{h}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}a_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\sim\Bin(N,\frac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A3.SS6.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we know</p>
<table id="A3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En[\widehat{\nu}_{h}(x,1)]=p_{N}\En\left[\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}(x)\right],\qquad p_{N}=(1+\lambda)\En_{A\sim\Bin(N,\frac{1}{2})}\left[\frac{A}{N+\lambda A}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En[\widehat{\nu}_{h}(x,1)]=p_{N}\En\left[\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}(x)\right],\qquad p_{N}=(1+\lambda)\En_{A\sim\Bin(N,\frac{1}{2})}\left[\frac{A}{N+\lambda A}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p8.4" class="ltx_p">Applying this equation recursively gives the desired result.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A3.SS6" title="C.6 Lower Bound for SMC with Exact Value Function ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>. </span>
We let <math id="A3.SS6.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=\frac{2A}{N}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=\frac{2A}{N}-1</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A3.SS6.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> symmetrically distributed on <math id="A3.SS6.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we can write</p>
<table id="A3.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{N}{N+\lambda A}=\frac{2}{2+\lambda(Y+1)}=\frac{2}{2+\lambda}\cdot\frac{1}{1+\frac{\lambda}{2+\lambda}Y}=\frac{2}{2+\lambda}\sum_{k\geq 0}(-1)^{k}\left(\frac{\lambda Y}{2+\lambda}\right)^{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{N}{N+\lambda A}=\frac{2}{2+\lambda(Y+1)}=\frac{2}{2+\lambda}\cdot\frac{1}{1+\frac{\lambda}{2+\lambda}Y}=\frac{2}{2+\lambda}\sum_{k\geq 0}(-1)^{k}\left(\frac{\lambda Y}{2+\lambda}\right)^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A3.SS6.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En Y^{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En Y^{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for odd integer <math id="A3.SS6.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En Y^{2}=\frac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En Y^{2}=\frac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can conclude</p>
<table id="A3.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left[\frac{N}{N+\lambda A}\right]\geq\frac{2}{2+\lambda}\left(1+\left(\frac{\lambda}{2+\lambda}\right)^{2}\frac{1}{N}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left[\frac{N}{N+\lambda A}\right]\geq\frac{2}{2+\lambda}\left(1+\left(\frac{\lambda}{2+\lambda}\right)^{2}\frac{1}{N}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p9.3" class="ltx_p">Reorganizing yields</p>
<table id="A3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{N}=(1+\lambda)\En\left[\frac{A}{N+\lambda A}\right]=\frac{1+\lambda}{\lambda}\left(1-\En\left[\frac{N}{N+\lambda A}\right]\right)\leq\frac{1+\lambda}{2+\lambda}-\frac{2\lambda(1+\lambda)}{(2+\lambda)^{3}N}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{N}=(1+\lambda)\En\left[\frac{A}{N+\lambda A}\right]=\frac{1+\lambda}{\lambda}\left(1-\En\left[\frac{N}{N+\lambda A}\right]\right)\leq\frac{1+\lambda}{2+\lambda}-\frac{2\lambda(1+\lambda)}{(2+\lambda)^{3}N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p9.4" class="ltx_p">∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs for SMC-RS</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Analogously to <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>,
we introduce the following quantity for <a href="#alg2" title="In 3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle W_{h}\vcentcolon=\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right],\qquad\widehat{W}_{h}\vcentcolon=\prod_{\ell=1}^{h}W_{\ell}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{h}\vcentcolon=\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right],\qquad\widehat{W}_{h}\vcentcolon=\prod_{\ell=1}^{h}W_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h}=\{\mathcal{S}_{1},\cdots,\mathcal{S}_{h}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h}=\{\mathcal{S}_{1},\cdots,\mathcal{S}_{h}\}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the full history of the execution of SMC-RS (<a href="#alg2" title="In 3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) up to the end of iteration <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. We write <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En_{h}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En_{h}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> to be the conditional distribution with respect to <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For step <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> of SMC-RS (<a href="#alg2" title="In 3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), given <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of i.i.d. samples from the distribution <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> given by</p>
<table id="A4.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}_{h}(x_{h})=\frac{1}{W_{h}}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(x_{h}\mid x_{h-1})\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right],\qquad\forall x_{h}\in\mathcal{X}_{h}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}_{h}(x_{h})=\frac{1}{W_{h}}\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1}}\left[\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(x_{h}\mid x_{h-1})\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right],\qquad\forall x_{h}\in\mathcal{X}_{h}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, for any <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{h}:\mathcal{X}_{h}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{h}:\mathcal{X}_{h}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\frac{1}{\widehat{Z}_{1}}\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{h}}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\frac{1}{\widehat{Z}_{1}}\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{h}}\left[\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>. </span>
The first claim follows immediately from the analysis of rejection sampling: For any <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}\in\mathcal{X}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}\in\mathcal{X}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, by Bayes’ rule, we have</p>
<table id="A4.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(x_{h}\mid\text{accept})\propto\mathbb{P}(\text{accept}\mid x_{h})\cdot\mathbb{P}(x_{h})\propto\widehat{\mu}_{h}(x_{h})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mtext>accept</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>accept</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(x_{h}\mid\text{accept})\propto\mathbb{P}(\text{accept}\mid x_{h})\cdot\mathbb{P}(x_{h})\propto\widehat{\mu}_{h}(x_{h}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the second claim, we prove the following result, from which <a href="#A4.E87" title="In Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">87</span></a> follows inductively:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E89.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\left[W_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\En_{h-1}\left[W_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\left[W_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\En_{h-1}\left[W_{h}\cdot\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}\left[g_{h}\right]\right]=\En_{x_{h-1}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h-1},x_{h}\sim\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{h-1})}\left[\frac{\widehat{V}(x_{h})g_{h}(x_{h})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]=\widehat{Z}_{h}/\widehat{Z}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]=\widehat{Z}_{h}/\widehat{Z}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A4.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{H}\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]=Z\cdot\pi^{\star}_{H}(x)/\widehat{Z}_{1},\qquad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{H}\widehat{\nu}_{H}(x)\right]=Z\cdot\pi^{\star}_{H}(x)/\widehat{Z}_{1},\qquad\forall x\in\mathcal{X}_{H}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Further, we define <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(x)=\frac{V^{\star}(x)}{\widehat{V}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(x)=\frac{V^{\star}(x)}{\widehat{V}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A4.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{h}=\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{h}=\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Then <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> with <math id="A4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=\rho(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=\rho(x)</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale with <math id="A4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{0}=Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{0}=Z</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{H}=\widehat{W}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{H}=\widehat{W}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, similar to <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we have the following upper bound.
<span id="A4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For <a href="#alg2" title="In 3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq\frac{1}{2Z}\En\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\rvert\leq\frac{1}{2Z}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq\frac{1}{2Z}\En\lvert\widehat{W}_{H}-Z\rvert\leq\frac{1}{2Z}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{h}-M_{h-1}=\widehat{W}_{h}\left(\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho]-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{h}-M_{h-1}=\widehat{W}_{h}\left(\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho]-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\nu}_{h}=\mathrm{unif}(\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>unif</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\nu}_{h}=\mathrm{unif}(\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of i.i.d samples from <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we can bound</p>
<table id="A4.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\lvert\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho_{h}]-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho_{h}]\rvert\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\lvert\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho_{h}]-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho_{h}]\rvert\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\En_{h-1}\left\lvert\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\rho(x_{h})-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right\rvert^{2}}=\sqrt{\frac{\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})^{2}]-\left(\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]\right)^{2}}{N}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\En_{h-1}\left\lvert\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\rho(x_{h})-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right\rvert^{2}}=\sqrt{\frac{\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})^{2}]-\left(\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]\right)^{2}}{N}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and hence</p>
<table id="A4.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{N}\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{N}\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E94.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\sqrt{\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})^{2}]-\left(\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]\right)^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\sqrt{\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})^{2}]-\left(\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]\right)^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E95.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]\left(\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})^{2}]\right]-\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\left(\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]\right)^{2}\right]\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]\left(\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})^{2}]\right]-\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\left(\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]\right)^{2}\right]\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E96.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\widehat{Z}_{h}\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{h}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}\right]-Z^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\widehat{Z}_{h}\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi_{h}}\left[\frac{V^{\star}(x_{h})^{2}}{\widehat{V}(x_{h})}\right]-Z^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E97.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~Z\sqrt{\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h}}\left[\frac{\pi^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{\pi}(x_{h})}\right]-1}=Z\sqrt{D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~Z\sqrt{\En_{x_{h}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h}}\left[\frac{\pi^{\star}(x_{h})}{\widehat{\pi}(x_{h})}\right]-1}=Z\sqrt{D_{\chi^{2}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\;\|\;{}\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the third line uses <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\left(\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]\right)^{2}\right]\geq\left(\En[\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]]\right)^{2}=Z^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\left(\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]\right)^{2}\right]\geq\left(\En[\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]]\right)^{2}=Z^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (Cauchy inequality and <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>), and the last line follows from the definition of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence.
Taking summation completes the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Analysis of SMC-RS with Heavy-tailed Errors</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parallel to SMC, we show that SMC-RS also enjoys an upper bound that depends only on coverage (<a href="#S3.SS1.SSS1" title="3.1.1 Handling Tail Behavior ‣ 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1.1</span></a>).
<span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{theorem}</span>
Under <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, suppose that SMC-RS (<a href="#alg2" title="In 3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) is instantiated with <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\geq\widehat{C}_{\mathsf{act}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\geq\widehat{C}_{\mathsf{act}}</annotation></semantics></math>. It holds that for any <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#alg2" title="In 3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> achieves</p>
<table id="A4.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E98.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq H\sqrt{\frac{M}{N}}+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathrm{Cov}_{M}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\En[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq H\sqrt{\frac{M}{N}}+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\mathrm{Cov}_{M}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The convergence rate of <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Analysis of SMC-RS with Heavy-tailed Errors ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> improves upon that of SMC (<a href="#S3.SS1.SSS1" title="3.1.1 Handling Tail Behavior ‣ 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1.1</span></a>) by a factor of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sf act}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sf act}</annotation></semantics></math>, though the same factor reappears in the time complexity. The expected time complexity bound matches <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We follow the proof of <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> (<a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>).
By <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Technical Tools ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\lvert\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho_{h}]-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho_{h}]\rvert=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En_{h-1}\lvert\En_{\widehat{\nu}_{h}}[\rho_{h}]-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho_{h}]\rvert=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E99.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\En_{h-1}\left\lvert\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\rho(x_{h})-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\En_{h-1}\left\lvert\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x_{h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}}\rho(x_{h})-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E100.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\frac{R}{N}\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]}+2R\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\{\rho(x_{h})\geq R\}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\frac{R}{N}\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]}+2R\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\{\rho(x_{h})\geq R\}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where we use <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d samples from <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we can bound</p>
<table id="A4.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E101.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{R}{N}}\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\sqrt{\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]}\right]+2\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\{\rho(x_{h})\geq R\}]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{R}{N}}\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\sqrt{\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]}\right]+2\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\{\rho(x_{h})\geq R\}]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Further, by <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A4.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\sqrt{\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]}\right]\leq\sqrt{\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]\En[\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]]}\leq\sqrt{\widehat{Z}_{h}\cdot Z}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\sqrt{\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]}\right]\leq\sqrt{\En[\widehat{W}_{h}]\En[\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})]]}\leq\sqrt{\widehat{Z}_{h}\cdot Z},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E103.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\{\rho(x_{h})\geq R\}]\right]=Z\cdot\mathbb{P}_{x\sim\pi^{\star}_{h}}\left(\rho(x_{h})\geq R\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\left[\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\En_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho(x_{h})\mathbb{I}\{\rho(x_{h})\geq R\}]\right]=Z\cdot\mathbb{P}_{x\sim\pi^{\star}_{h}}\left(\rho(x_{h})\geq R\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Choosing <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=M\frac{Z}{\widehat{Z}_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=M\frac{Z}{\widehat{Z}_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A4.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E104.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\leq 2Z\sqrt{\frac{M}{N}}+2Z\mathrm{Cov}_{M}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Z</mi><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Z</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>o</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\En\lvert M_{h}-M_{h-1}\rvert\leq 2Z\sqrt{\frac{M}{N}}+2Z\mathrm{Cov}_{M}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Taking summation completes the proof.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Faster Convergence for SMC-RS</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present and analyze a modification of SMC-RS, which we call SMC-RS with restart (<a href="#alg3" title="In D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). Under the following assumption, we prove that <a href="#alg3" title="In D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> achieves exponential convergence (analogous to <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Beyond SMC: Faster Convergence under 𝐿_∞-condition ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> for SMC).
<span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{assumption}</span>
There are at most <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> values of <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(x_{h+1}\mid x_{h})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(x_{h+1}\mid x_{h})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and these are efficiently enumerable.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> Diffusion Monte Carlo</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Transition kernel <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, value function <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter:</span> initial sample size <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            Initialize <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="alg3.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⟂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\perp</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1,\cdots,H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1,\cdots,H</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              For each <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, compute <math id="alg3.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{V}(x_{h-1})=\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h})\mid{}x_{h-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{V}(x_{h-1})=\En_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}(x_{h})\mid{}x_{h-1}]</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Define <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{h-1}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x_{h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}}\frac{\widetilde{V}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{h-1}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{x_{h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}}\frac{\widetilde{V}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Define the weighted empirical measure <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}_{h-1}=\frac{1}{NW_{h-1}}\sum_{x_{h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}}\frac{\widetilde{V}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\updelta_{x_{h-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}_{h-1}=\frac{1}{NW_{h-1}}\sum_{x_{h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}}\frac{\widetilde{V}(x_{h-1})}{\widehat{V}(x_{h-1})}\updelta_{x_{h-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Generates <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\sim\widetilde{\mu}_{h-1},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\sim\widehat{\pi}(\cdot\mid{}\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\sim\widetilde{\mu}_{h-1},x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\sim\widehat{\pi}(\cdot\mid{}\tilde{x}_{h-1}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})</annotation></semantics></math> independently for <math id="alg3.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Define <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}=\{x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\}_{i\in[N]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}=\{x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}}\}_{i\in[N]}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg3.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\nu}_{h}=\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\nu}_{h}=\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            Define <math id="alg3.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{W}_{H}=\prod_{h=1}^{H}W_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{W}_{H}=\prod_{h=1}^{H}W_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> With probability <math id="alg3.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\left\{\frac{\widehat{W}_{H}}{\widetilde{Z}_{1}},1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\left\{\frac{\widehat{W}_{H}}{\widetilde{Z}_{1}},1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, output <math id="alg3.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\widehat{\nu}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\widehat{\nu}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, and otherwise restart the algorithm.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the following guarantee:
<span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{theorem}</span>
Suppose that <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> hold, and we denote <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\vcentcolon=\mathsf{C}_{\infty}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\vcentcolon=\mathsf{C}_{\infty}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, suppose that we have <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\leq\widetilde{Z}_{1}\leq JZ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\leq\widetilde{Z}_{1}\leq JZ</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <a href="#alg3" title="In D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> with <span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output Option 2</span> samples from a distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies</p>
<table id="A4.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\mu,\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq\delta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\mu,\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)\leq\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">as long as <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq\Omega(H\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}\log(JH/\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq\Omega(H\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}\log(JH/\delta))</annotation></semantics></math>, using a number of outer loop steps that is bounded by <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(J^{2}\log(1/\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(J^{2}\log(1/\delta))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Under <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>, we can always choose <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Z}_{1}=\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}_{1}=\mathsf{C}_{\infty}\widehat{Z}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\leq\widetilde{Z}_{1}\leq\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\leq\widetilde{Z}_{1}\leq\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}Z</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, we can run <a href="#alg3" title="In D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> 1 time solely for estimating <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, with choice <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Z}_{1}=2\widehat{W}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Z}_{1}=2\widehat{W}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\leq\widetilde{Z}\leq 4Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\leq\widetilde{Z}\leq 4Z</annotation></semantics></math> with high probability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the proof of <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Beyond SMC: Faster Convergence under 𝐿_∞-condition ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we first state and prove the following lemma (as an analogue to <a href="#A3.SS5" title="C.5 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>). <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> then follows from the argument in <a href="#A3.SS5" title="C.5 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>.
<span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
Under the condition of <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>, for any <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if we run SMC-RS (<a href="#alg3" title="In D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) with <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\Omega(H\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}\log(H/\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\Omega(H\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}\log(H/\delta))</annotation></semantics></math> particles, then with probability at least <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|\leq Z/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|\leq Z/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Faster Convergence for SMC-RS ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>. </span>
We follow the proof of <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> (<a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix D Proofs for SMC-RS ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>). Recall that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{M_{h}-M_{h-1}}{\widehat{W}_{h}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{M_{h}-M_{h-1}}{\widehat{W}_{h}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E106.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\rho(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\rho(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}},\cdots,x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}},\cdots,x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples from <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> (given <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Note that by <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, it holds that <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(x_{h})-1\in[-\epsilon,\epsilon]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(x_{h})-1\in[-\epsilon,\epsilon]</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{h}\in\mathcal{X}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{h}\in\mathcal{X}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies that <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[e^{\lambda(\rho(x_{h})-\mathbb{E}_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho])}]\leq e^{\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}/8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x_{h}\sim\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[e^{\lambda(\rho(x_{h})-\mathbb{E}_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho])}]\leq e^{\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}/8}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</p>
<table id="A4.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}[\exp(\lambda(M_{h}-M_{h-1}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}[\exp(\lambda(M_{h}-M_{h-1}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E108.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}\left[\exp\left(\lambda\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\rho(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right)\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{h-1}\left[\exp\left(\lambda\widehat{W}_{h}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{N}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\rho(x_{h}^{{\scriptscriptstyle i}})-\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\right)\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\exp\left(\frac{1}{N}\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}\widehat{W}_{h}^{2}\right)}\leq{\exp\left(\frac{1}{N}\lambda^{2}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}M_{h-1}^{2}\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\exp\left(\frac{1}{N}\lambda^{2}\epsilon^{2}\widehat{W}_{h}^{2}\right)}\leq{\exp\left(\frac{1}{N}\lambda^{2}\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}M_{h-1}^{2}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">where we use <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{h-1}=\En_{h-1}[M_{h}]=\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\geq\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{-1}\widehat{W}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{h-1}=\En_{h-1}[M_{h}]=\widehat{W}_{h}\En_{\widehat{\mu}_{h}}[\rho]\geq\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{-1}\widehat{W}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">By Freedman’s inequality, it follows that for any <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|M_{h}-Z|\leq\sum_{i=1}^{h-1}\frac{\lambda\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}M_{i}^{2}}{N}+\frac{\log(2/\delta)}{\lambda}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|M_{h}-Z|\leq\sum_{i=1}^{h-1}\frac{\lambda\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}M_{i}^{2}}{N}+\frac{\log(2/\delta)}{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Choosing <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=4\log(2H/\delta)/Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=4\log(2H/\delta)/Z</annotation></semantics></math> and using the union bound, it follows that with probability <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|M_{h}-Z|\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|M_{h}-Z|\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{4\log(2/\delta)\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{N}\sum_{i=0}^{h-1}\frac{M_{i}^{2}}{Z}+\frac{Z}{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>Z</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{4\log(2/\delta)\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2}}{N}\sum_{i=0}^{h-1}\frac{M_{i}^{2}}{Z}+\frac{Z}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Since we have chosen <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\Omega(H\log(H/\delta)\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\Omega(H\log(H/\delta)\mathsf{C}_{\infty}^{2}\epsilon^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows from induction on <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> that in the event that <a href="#A3.E71" title="In C.5 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a> holds, we have that <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|M_{h}-Z|\leq Z/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|M_{h}-Z|\leq Z/2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, this implies that <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|\leq Z/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|\leq Z/2</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our main theoretical results demonstrated that particle filtering methods like SMC can achieve strong guarantees under the same assumptions on <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}</annotation></semantics></math> as the backtracking-based method VGB introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite> — while improving parallel runtime from <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(H^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(H^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{O}(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{O}(H)</annotation></semantics></math>. In this section, we show that the connection goes deeper: for <em id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">any</em> problem instance, the execution of VGB can be <em id="A5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">coupled</em> with the execution of <span id="A5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span>, a variant of SMC in which the children of each particle are sampled independently.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We defer formal definitions until after stating the result (<a href="#A5" title="Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>), but we make several remarks for context. Henceforth, we specify to the autoregressive setting (<a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminaries ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) in which VGB was defined <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite>. Recall that VGB implements a single-particle random walk in which the allowed transitions can not only add a token to the current particle (i.e. <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}\mapsto a_{1:h+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}\mapsto a_{1:h+1}</annotation></semantics></math>) but also backtrack (i.e. <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}\mapsto a_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}\mapsto a_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>). For technical reasons, we augment the state space of the random walk with a state <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math> that is only adjacent to the empty string <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⟂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\perp</annotation></semantics></math>. See <a href="#A5.SS2" title="E.2 Definition of SMC-IND ‣ Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> and <a href="#A5.SS1" title="E.1 Background on VGB ‣ Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> for the formal definitions of <span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span> and the VGB random walk.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{theorem}</span>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\mathsf{DMC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>𝖣𝖬𝖢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\mathsf{DMC}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the (random) multiset of particles visited by <span id="A5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span> with <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> initial particles. Let <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\mathsf{VGB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\mathsf{VGB}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the (random) multiset of particles visited by VGB (initialized at <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math>) before the <math id="A5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N+1</annotation></semantics></math>-st visit to <math id="A5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is a coupling so that <math id="A5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\mathsf{DMC}}=\mathcal{S}_{\mathsf{VGB}}\setminus\{\mathfrak{s}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>𝖣𝖬𝖢</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔰</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\mathsf{DMC}}=\mathcal{S}_{\mathsf{VGB}}\setminus\{\mathfrak{s}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (with multiplicity) almost surely.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, each particle <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}</annotation></semantics></math> visited by <span id="A5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">SMC-IND</span> corresponds to an interval of time in which the VGB random walk started at <math id="A5.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}</annotation></semantics></math>, ended at <math id="A5.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and never visited the parent node <math id="A5.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (where we take the parent of <math id="A5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⟂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\perp</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="A5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math>). This demonstrates that the paradigm of backtracking to tame error amplification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite> is, in a sense, equivalent to a form of particle filtering.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Outline of appendix</h5>

<div id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A5.SS1" title="E.1 Background on VGB ‣ Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> we introduce the VGB random walk (slightly modified for technical reasons). In <a href="#A5.SS2" title="E.2 Definition of SMC-IND ‣ Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> we introduce the <span id="A5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span> stochastic process. In <a href="#A5.SS3" title="E.3 Coupling VGB with SMC-IND ‣ Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a> we prove <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Background on VGB</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The (non-lazy) VGB random walk <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite> is defined on state space <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}=\mathcal{X}_{0}\sqcup\dots\sqcup\mathcal{X}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}=\mathcal{X}_{0}\sqcup\dots\sqcup\mathcal{X}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is the token space and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{h}:=\mathcal{A}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{h}:=\mathcal{A}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. For technical convenience (specifically, to avoid casework at step <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> when coupling VGB with <span id="A5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span>), we introduce an auxiliary state <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math> that is not in the original definition. We define the transition kernel <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows. First, <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math> always transitions to <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⟂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\perp</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.E112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E112.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(\perp\mid{}\mathfrak{s})=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝔰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(\perp\mid{}\mathfrak{s})=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(112)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Second, any <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}\in\mathcal{A}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}\in\mathcal{A}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq h&lt;H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq h&lt;H</annotation></semantics></math> can transition to either a “child” <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h+1}</annotation></semantics></math> or the “parent” <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.E113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E113.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(a_{1:h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})=\frac{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h+1})}{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})+\sum_{a_{h+1}^{\prime}}\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}^{\prime}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h},a_{h+1}^{\prime})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(a_{1:h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})=\frac{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h+1})}{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})+\sum_{a_{h+1}^{\prime}}\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}^{\prime}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h},a_{h+1}^{\prime})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(113)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A5.E114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E114.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(a_{1:h-1}\mid{}a_{1:h})=\frac{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})+\sum_{a_{h+1}^{\prime}}\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}^{\prime}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h},a_{h+1}^{\prime})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(a_{1:h-1}\mid{}a_{1:h})=\frac{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})}{\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})+\sum_{a_{h+1}^{\prime}}\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}^{\prime}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h},a_{h+1}^{\prime})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(114)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with the convention that <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:0}=\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">⟂</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:0}=\perp</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. the empty string) and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:-1}=\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:-1}=\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Third, any <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:H}\in\mathcal{A}^{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:H}\in\mathcal{A}^{H}</annotation></semantics></math> must transition to its parent:</p>
<table id="A5.E115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E115.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(a_{1:H-1}\mid{}a_{1:H})=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(a_{1:H-1}\mid{}a_{1:H})=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(115)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The transition kernel of the original VGB random walk <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite> is identical conditioned on never visiting <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, since <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is only reachable from <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⟂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\perp</annotation></semantics></math> (and only transitions to <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⟂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\perp</annotation></semantics></math>), our modification only affects the execution of VGB by stochastically inserting copies of the sequence <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathfrak{s},\perp)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔰</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathfrak{s},\perp)</annotation></semantics></math> into VGB’s random trajectory.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For notational convenience, it is useful to define a transition kernel <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{down}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖽𝗈𝗐𝗇</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{down}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the VGB transition kernel conditioned on “downward” moves, i.e.</p>
<table id="A5.E116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E116.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{down}}(a_{1:h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})=\frac{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h+1})}{\sum_{a_{h+1}^{\prime}}\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}^{\prime}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h},a_{h+1}^{\prime})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖽𝗈𝗐𝗇</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{down}}(a_{1:h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})=\frac{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h+1})}{\sum_{a_{h+1}^{\prime}}\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{h+1}^{\prime}\mid{}a_{1:h})\widehat{V}(a_{1:h},a_{h+1}^{\prime})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(116)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Definition of <span id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span></h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#alg4" title="In E.2 Definition of SMC-IND ‣ Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we describe how <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span> stochastically constructs multisets of particles <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> for a given problem instance. Note that there is no specified output mechanism, since the coupling between <span id="A5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span> and VGB will apply to the entire multiset of particles.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg4" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span> Sequential Monte Carlo with Independent Sampling (<span id="alg4.5" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span>)</figcaption>
<div id="alg4.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg4.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Autoregressive language model <math id="alg4.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, value function <math id="alg4.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg4.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter:</span> initial sample size <math id="alg4.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg4.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            Initialize <math id="alg4.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="alg4.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="alg4.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⟂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\perp</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg4.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
            <span id="alg4.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1,\cdots,H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1,\cdots,H</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              Initialize a multi-set <math id="alg4.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}=\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}=\{\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg4.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg4.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               Sample <math id="alg4.l7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D\sim\Geom(\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(a_{1:h-2}\mid{}a_{1:h-1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Geom</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\sim\Geom(\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{VGB}}(a_{1:h-2}\mid{}a_{1:h-1}))</annotation></semantics></math> (with convention <math id="alg4.l7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:-1}=\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:-1}=\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math>; see <a href="#A5.SS1" title="E.1 Background on VGB ‣ Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>)

</div>
<div id="alg4.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <span id="alg4.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg4.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq D</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg4.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg4.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 Sample <math id="alg4.l9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}\sim\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{down}}(\cdot\mid{}a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖽𝗈𝗐𝗇</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}\sim\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{down}}(\cdot\mid{}a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg4.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
                 Update <math id="alg4.l10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}_{h}\cup\{a_{1:h}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}_{h}\cup\{a_{1:h}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
     
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Coupling VGB with <span id="A5.SS3.2" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span></h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We interpret the executions of <span id="A5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span> and VGB as stochastically constructing forests of particles. We then show that these forests are actually the same (up to occurrences of <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math>) when the randomness is appropriately coupled.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Infinite-particle <span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span> process</h5>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The execution of <span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span> with <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> naturally defines a rooted forest <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖣𝖬𝖢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}</annotation></semantics></math> where each node is labelled by a particle in <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0}\sqcup\dots\sqcup\mathcal{S}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⊔</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0}\sqcup\dots\sqcup\mathcal{S}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. The roots are the particles in <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the parent of a particle in <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is the particle in <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math> that birthed it. Note that there may be multiple (or even infinitely many) occurrences of any particle <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖣𝖬𝖢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}</annotation></semantics></math> may contain multiple nodes with the same label. The parent of a node labelled <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}</annotation></semantics></math> always has label <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Infinite-time VGB process</h5>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We next show how an execution of VGB in the autoregressive tree <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> can be interpreted as a rooted tree <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}</annotation></semantics></math>, similar to above. Fix an infinite trajectory <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{0},x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},\dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{0},x_{1},x_{2},x_{3},\dots)</annotation></semantics></math> of VGB with <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}=\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}=\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose that <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math> occurs infinitely often in the trajectory. The root node of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}</annotation></semantics></math> is indexed by <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and labeled <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Every other node is indexed by an interval <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t,t^{\prime}]\subset\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t,t^{\prime}]\subset\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> with the property that <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t-1}=x_{t^{\prime}+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t-1}=x_{t^{\prime}+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the parent of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}=x_{t^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}=x_{t^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and this parent does not occur within <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{t},x_{t+1},\dots,x_{t^{\prime}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{t},x_{t+1},\dots,x_{t^{\prime}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This node is labeled with <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and its parent in <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique node with label <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> whose interval contains <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t,t^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t,t^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Suppose that VGB almost surely visits <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math> infinitely often. There is a coupling of the randomness of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖣𝖬𝖢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖣𝖬𝖢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}</annotation></semantics></math> is almost surely equal to the forest <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}\setminus\{\mathfrak{s}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝔰</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}\setminus\{\mathfrak{s}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We construct the coupling layer by layer. By the lemma assumption, it is clear that the first layer of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖣𝖬𝖢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}</annotation></semantics></math> is almost surely identical to that of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now fix <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and condition on the forest structure and labels <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (but not the indices <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t,t^{\prime}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t,t^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math> themselves) of the first <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> layers of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix any node <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math> with label <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the law of the VGB random walk between these two visits to <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The walk is restricted to the subtree rooted at <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, but since the walk is Markovian, its law is otherwise unchanged by the conditioning (and it is also independent of the children of other nodes <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota^{\prime}\neq\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ι</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota^{\prime}\neq\iota</annotation></semantics></math> at layer <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>). Let <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p=\mathbb{P}(a_{1:h-2}\mid{}a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\mathbb{P}(a_{1:h-2}\mid{}a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> (with the convention <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-2}=\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-2}=\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math>). The number of children <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of times that the walk goes to a child of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-1}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> before it returns to <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h-2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[D^{\prime}=k]=(1-p)^{k}p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[D^{\prime}=k]=(1-p)^{k}p</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{0,1,2,\dots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{0,1,2,\dots\}</annotation></semantics></math>. That is, <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a geometric random variable with success probability <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the label of each child of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math> is independent and distributed according to <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{down}}(\cdot\mid{}a_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>𝖽𝗈𝗐𝗇</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{down}}(\cdot\mid{}a_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the coupling can be extended to the children of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>. </span>
The first <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> trees of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖣𝖬𝖢</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{DMC}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be coupled to the forest induced by <span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text">SMC-IND</span> with <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> initial particles. Similarly, the first <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> trees of <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖵𝖦𝖡</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{VGB}}</annotation></semantics></math> correspond exactly to the prefix of the trajectory of VGB before <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is visited <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N+1</annotation></semantics></math> times. The claim then follows from <a href="#A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" title="Infinite-time VGB process ‣ E.3 Coupling VGB with SMC-IND ‣ Appendix E A Unified Perspective on Backtracking and Particle Filtering ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Limits of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a></h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix we formally state the requisite definitions for <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Limits of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, and prove the theorem. In <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Myopic Particle Filtering Algorithms ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>, we formalize the definition of a myopic particle filtering algorithm. In <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Specialized Setting and Formal Theorem Statement ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a> we state <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Specialized Setting and Formal Theorem Statement ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>, which directly implies <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Limits of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>. In <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>, we provide intuition for and formally prove <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Specialized Setting and Formal Theorem Statement ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Myopic Particle Filtering Algorithms</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{definition}</span>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A <em id="A6.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">myopic particle filtering algorithm with <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> particles</em> is defined as follows. The algorithm computes a stochastic sequence of multisets <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}\subset\mathcal{A}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}\subset\mathcal{A}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq h\leq H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq h\leq H</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfying the following properties:</p>
<ol id="A6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It holds almost surely that for all <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq h\leq H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq h\leq H</annotation></semantics></math>, for each <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:h}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:h-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}_{h}|\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}_{h}|\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The law of <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{1:h}):a_{1:h}\in\mathcal{A}^{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{1:h}):a_{1:h}\in\mathcal{A}^{h})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\widehat{V}(a_{1:k}):a_{1:k}\in\mathcal{A}^{k},k\leq h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{V}(a_{1:k}):a_{1:k}\in\mathcal{A}^{k},k\leq h)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The algorithm then (stochastically) outputs any element of <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The first condition is a natural formalization of what it means to be a particle filtering method, i.e. a particle in <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot appear “out of nowhere”; rather, it must have a parent in <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The second condition asserts that the number of particles is always at most <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. The third condition is the “myopic” condition, which enforces that, at the level of distributions, the algorithm does not use information from later steps <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;h</annotation></semantics></math> to determine the multiset <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{remark}</span>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">[Sequential Monte Carlo and variants]
It is straightforward from <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to see that Sequential Monte Carlo is indeed a myopic particle filtering algorithm, as is Sequential Monte Carlo with Rejection Sampling (<a href="#alg2" title="In 3.3 Beyond SMC: Near-perfect PRM ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{remark}</span>
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">[Computational efficiency]
We remark that <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Myopic Particle Filtering Algorithms ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a> does not enforce any bound on computational efficiency or query complexity; in particular, a myopic particle filtering algorithm is allowed to examine <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}\in\mathcal{A}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}\in\mathcal{A}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> before deciding on the set of particles <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>; it is not restricted to e.g. only querying the children of particles in <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. This only makes our impossibility result stronger. That said, it is an interesting open question to prove an analogous result to <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Limits of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> that applies to <em id="A6.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> algorithms that make <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(H^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(H^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> queries to <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Such a result would be formally incomparable to <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Limits of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Specialized Setting and Formal Theorem Statement</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since we are proving a lower bound, it suffices to consider a special case of the general setting from <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminaries ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Thus, we restrict to the autoregressive generation setting (<a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminaries ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and moreover set <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{ref}}:=\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{ref}}:=\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{H})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We define a problem instance by specifying some distribution <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\Delta(\mathcal{A}^{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\Delta(\mathcal{A}^{H})</annotation></semantics></math> and functions <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu_{h})_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu_{h})_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{h}:\mathcal{A}^{h}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>h</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{h}:\mathcal{A}^{h}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>. These induce <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\star},\widehat{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\star},\widehat{V}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A6.E117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E117.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V^{\star}(a_{1:h}):=\frac{\mu(a_{1:h})}{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{1:h})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\star}(a_{1:h}):=\frac{\mu(a_{1:h})}{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{1:h})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(117)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A6.E118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E118.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{V}(a_{1:h}):=\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{h}(a_{1:h})}{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{1:h})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}(a_{1:h}):=\frac{\widehat{\mu}_{h}(a_{1:h})}{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}(a_{1:h})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(118)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Note that the goal distribution <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, and the third condition of <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Myopic Particle Filtering Algorithms ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a> precisely enforces that the law of <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{\mu}_{0},\dots,\widehat{\mu}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\mu}_{0},\dots,\widehat{\mu}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>. For <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> to hold with parameter <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sf act}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sf act}</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to have <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu(a_{h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\leq C_{\sf act}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>𝖺𝖼𝗍</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(a_{h+1}\mid{}a_{1:h})\leq C_{\sf act}/2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h+1}\in\mathcal{A}^{h+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h+1}\in\mathcal{A}^{h+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> holds with parameter <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{C}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{C}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{C}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖢</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{C}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate for <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> in the following sense:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{definition}</span>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We say that <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate for <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\Delta(\mathcal{A}^{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\Delta(\mathcal{A}^{H})</annotation></semantics></math> if it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.E119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E119.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\widehat{\mu}(a_{1:h})}{\mu(a_{1:h})}\in[1/\kappa,\kappa]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\widehat{\mu}(a_{1:h})}{\mu(a_{1:h})}\in[1/\kappa,\kappa]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(119)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}\in\mathcal{A}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}\in\mathcal{A}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and moreover <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mu}(a_{1:H})=\mu(a_{1:H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}(a_{1:H})=\mu(a_{1:H})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:H}\in\mathcal{A}^{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:H}\in\mathcal{A}^{H}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We can now formally state the main result of this appendix, which directly implies <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Limits of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{theorem}</span>
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(H):=\log(H)/(4\log\log(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(H):=\log(H)/(4\log\log(H))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. There is no myopic particle filtering algorithm <span id="A6.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> with the following guarantee: fix <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large. <span id="A6.SS2.p5.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> uses at most <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(H)</annotation></semantics></math> particles. For any <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\Delta(\mathcal{A}^{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\Delta(\mathcal{A}^{H})</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}:\mathcal{A}^{\leq H}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}:\mathcal{A}^{\leq H}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the execution of <span id="A6.SS2.p5.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> on <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> has output <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="o_{1:H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{1:H}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="A6.E120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E120.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{o_{1:H}\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o_{1:H}\in\mathcal{E}]\geq H^{-1/5}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Alg</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{o_{1:H}\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o_{1:H}\in\mathcal{E}]\geq H^{-1/5}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(120)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">for all events <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}\subset\mathcal{A}^{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}\subset\mathcal{A}^{H}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\mathcal{E})\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\mathcal{E})\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Limits of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>. </span>
Immediate from <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Specialized Setting and Formal Theorem Statement ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a> and the preceding discussion on <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Specialized Setting and Formal Theorem Statement ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a></h3>

<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.3.1 </span>Intuition and Formal Construction</h4>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Specialized Setting and Formal Theorem Statement ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>, we construct a family of problem instances (each specified by a choice of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{0},\dots,\widehat{\mu}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{0},\dots,\widehat{\mu}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>) such that any myopic particle filtering algorithm with at most <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> particles must fail on at least one instance in the family. We do so recursively, by first constructing an instance for <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and so forth. The analysis will be similarly inductive.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be a function to be determined. Assume that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}(N)</annotation></semantics></math> is a multiple of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})\in\Delta(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})\in\Delta(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star}):\mathcal{A}^{\leq\mathfrak{H}(N)}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star}):\mathcal{A}^{\leq\mathfrak{H}(N)}\to\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> recursively (in <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>) as follows.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Intuition for construction</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we provide intuition for the <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math> construction, which essentially follows Example 3.2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rohatgi et al. (2025)</a></cite>. We will have <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> be a product distribution where the marginal <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> is biased towards <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will then have <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> be “delayed” compared to <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. the marginal at step <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is biased towards <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{h-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{h-1}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the data of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}_{1}(\cdot;y^{\star}),\dots,\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}_{h}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}_{1}(\cdot;y^{\star}),\dots,\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}_{h}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and so as formalized in <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS2" title="F.3.2 Base Case for Analysis ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.2</span></a>, any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-particle myopic particle filtering method must incur large sampling error.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we provide intuition for the <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> construction. The horizon <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\mathfrak{H}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\mathfrak{H}(N)</annotation></semantics></math> is divided into blocks of size <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2</annotation></semantics></math>. Again <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> is a product distribution where the marginal at step <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is biased towards <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. In block <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[iK+1,(i+1)K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[iK+1,(i+1)K]</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> by “delaying” the dependence on <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{iK+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{iK+1}</annotation></semantics></math> to step <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i+1)K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i+1)K</annotation></semantics></math>, and embedding a copy of the <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-particle construction in the intervening steps. Intuitively, any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-particle myopic particle filtering algorithm has two choices at step <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="iK+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">iK+1</annotation></semantics></math>: either irrevocably guess <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{iK+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{iK+1}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. all particles <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{S}_{iK+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{S}_{iK+1}</annotation></semantics></math> will have the same value of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{iK+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{iK+1}</annotation></semantics></math>), or split up the particles so that some have different values of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{iK+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{iK+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The basic idea, formalized in <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS3" title="F.3.3 Inductive Step for Analysis ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.3</span></a>, is that both choices lead to sampling error: the former because no data about <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{iK+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{iK+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is available at step <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="iK+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">iK+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the latter by the inductive hypothesis on the <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-particle construction. The multiple blocks are needed to amplify the error induced by the first choice.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Making this argument precise requires a careful probabilistic analysis to ensure that the errors in the two cases cannot “cancel out”. Before proceeding to this analysis, we make the construction formal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\dots\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\dots\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of parameters to be determined later.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Formal construction: base case (<math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math>)</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Write <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\mathfrak{H}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\mathfrak{H}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. We define</p>
<table id="A6.E121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E121.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star}):=(1/2-\gamma_{1})^{\mathbb{I}[y_{h}\neq y^{\star}_{h}]}(1/2+\gamma_{1})^{\mathbb{I}[y_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star}):=(1/2-\gamma_{1})^{\mathbb{I}[y_{h}\neq y^{\star}_{h}]}(1/2+\gamma_{1})^{\mathbb{I}[y_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(121)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A6.E122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E122.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star}):=\begin{cases}1/2&amp;\text{ if }h=1\\
\mu_{1}(y_{h-1}\mid{}y_{1:h-2};y^{\star})&amp;\text{ if }1&lt;h&lt;H\\
2\mu_{1}(y_{H-1:H}\mid{}y_{1:H-2};y^{\star})&amp;\text{ if }h=\mathfrak{H}(1)\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star}):=\begin{cases}1/2&amp;\text{ if }h=1\\
\mu_{1}(y_{h-1}\mid{}y_{1:h-2};y^{\star})&amp;\text{ if }1&lt;h&lt;H\\
2\mu_{1}(y_{H-1:H}\mid{}y_{1:H-2};y^{\star})&amp;\text{ if }h=\mathfrak{H}(1)\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(122)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Formal construction: recursive case (<math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>)</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2</annotation></semantics></math>. For any nonnegative integer <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[\mathfrak{H}(N)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[\mathfrak{H}(N)]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="iK&lt;h\leq(i+1)K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">iK&lt;h\leq(i+1)K</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A6.E123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E123.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star}):=\begin{cases}(1/2-\gamma_{N})^{\mathbb{I}[y_{h}\neq y^{\star}_{h}]}(1/2+\gamma_{N})^{\mathbb{I}[y_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}]}&amp;\text{ if }h=iK+1\text{ or }h=(i+1)K\\
\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{iK+2:h-1};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})&amp;\text{ otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext> otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star}):=\begin{cases}(1/2-\gamma_{N})^{\mathbb{I}[y_{h}\neq y^{\star}_{h}]}(1/2+\gamma_{N})^{\mathbb{I}[y_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}]}&amp;\text{ if }h=iK+1\text{ or }h=(i+1)K\\
\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{iK+2:h-1};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})&amp;\text{ otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(123)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A6.E124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E124.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star}):=\begin{cases}1/2&amp;\text{ if }h=iK+1\\
\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{iK+2:h-1};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})&amp;\text{ if }iK+1&lt;h&lt;(i+1)K\\
2\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{(i+1)K}\mid{}y_{1:(i+1)K-1};y^{\star})&amp;\text{ if }h=(i+1)K\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star}):=\begin{cases}1/2&amp;\text{ if }h=iK+1\\
\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{iK+2:h-1};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})&amp;\text{ if }iK+1&lt;h&lt;(i+1)K\\
2\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{(i+1)K}\mid{}y_{1:(i+1)K-1};y^{\star})&amp;\text{ if }h=(i+1)K\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(124)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the following lemma we check that the desired accuracy condition is satisfied for all <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(3\sum_{i=1}^{N}\gamma_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(3\sum_{i=1}^{N}\gamma_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>-accurate for <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We proceed by induction on <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\mathfrak{H}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\mathfrak{H}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. We observe that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{1:H};y^{\star})=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{1:H};y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{1:H};y^{\star})=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{1:H};y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> and, for any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&lt;H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&lt;H</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{1:h};y^{\star})}{\mu_{1}(y_{1:h};y^{\star})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{1:h};y^{\star})}{\mu_{1}(y_{1:h};y^{\star})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E125.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(y_{h}\mid{}y_{1:h-1};y^{\star})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(125)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in[1/(1+2\gamma_{1}),1/(1-2\gamma_{1})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in[1/(1+2\gamma_{1}),1/(1-2\gamma_{1})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(126)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in[e^{-3\gamma_{1}},e^{3\gamma_{1}}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in[e^{-3\gamma_{1}},e^{3\gamma_{1}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(127)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and suppose that the claim holds for <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Set <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\mathfrak{H}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\mathfrak{H}(N)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=(i+1)K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=(i+1)K</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A6.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E128.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1:(i+1)K}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1:(i+1)K}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(128)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E129.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\left(\prod_{h^{\prime}=iK+2}^{(i+1)K-1}\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{h^{\prime}}\mid{}y_{iK+2:h^{\prime}-1};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\left(\prod_{h^{\prime}=iK+2}^{(i+1)K-1}\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{h^{\prime}}\mid{}y_{iK+2:h^{\prime}-1};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(129)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E130.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\cdot 2\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{(i+1)K}\mid{}y_{1:(i+1)K-1};y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\cdot 2\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{(i+1)K}\mid{}y_{1:(i+1)K-1};y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
