<tbody id="A6.E133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E133.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1:(i+1)K}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1:(i+1)K}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(133)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, it holds that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:(i+1)K};y^{\star})=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:(i+1)K};y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:(i+1)K};y^{\star})=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:(i+1)K};y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, and in particular, <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:H};y^{\star})=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:H};y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:H};y^{\star})=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:H};y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="iK+1\leq h&lt;(i+1)K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">iK+1\leq h&lt;(i+1)K</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A6.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E134.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:h};y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:h};y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E134.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1:h}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1:h}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(134)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E135.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{iK+2:h};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{iK+2:h};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(135)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E136.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in[e^{-3\sum_{n=1}^{N-1}\gamma_{n}},e^{3\sum_{n=1}^{N-1}\gamma_{n}}]\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{iK+2:h};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in[e^{-3\sum_{n=1}^{N-1}\gamma_{n}},e^{3\sum_{n=1}^{N-1}\gamma_{n}}]\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{iK+2:h};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(136)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E137.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in[e^{-3\sum_{n=1}^{N}\gamma_{n}},e^{3\sum_{n=1}^{N}\gamma_{n}}]\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{iK+2:h};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in[e^{-3\sum_{n=1}^{N}\gamma_{n}},e^{3\sum_{n=1}^{N}\gamma_{n}}]\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{iK+1}\mid{}y_{1:iK};y^{\star})\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(y_{iK+2:h};y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(137)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E138.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\in[e^{-3\sum_{n=1}^{N}\gamma_{n}},e^{3\sum_{n=1}^{N}\gamma_{n}}]\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:h};y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in[e^{-3\sum_{n=1}^{N}\gamma_{n}},e^{3\sum_{n=1}^{N}\gamma_{n}}]\cdot\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(y_{1:h};y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(138)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">which completes the proof.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To show that any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-particle myopic particle filtering method fails to cover <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> (for some choice of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>), we will show that there are events <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> that are extremely likely under <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> (for any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>) but extremely unlikely under the execution of any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-particle myopic particle filtering method (for a uniformly random choice of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>). <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3" title="Formal construction: recursive case (𝑁&gt;1) ‣ F.3.1 Intuition and Formal Construction ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.1</span></a> formally defines these events. <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3" title="Formal construction: recursive case (𝑁&gt;1) ‣ F.3.1 Intuition and Formal Construction ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.1</span></a> formalizes the claim about these events that we will prove inductively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{definition}</span>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">[Key events for analysis]
Fix <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\mathfrak{H}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\mathfrak{H}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. We define</p>
<table id="A6.E139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E139.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{1}(y^{\star}):=\{o_{1:H}:\#\{1&lt;h&lt;H:o_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}\}\geq(1/2+\gamma_{1}/2)(H-2)\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{1}(y^{\star}):=\{o_{1:H}:\#\{1&lt;h&lt;H:o_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}\}\geq(1/2+\gamma_{1}/2)(H-2)\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(139)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H:=\mathfrak{H}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H:=\mathfrak{H}(N)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2</annotation></semantics></math>. We define sets <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A6.E140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\circ}_{N}(y^{\star}):=\bigcap_{i}\left\{o_{1:H}:o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\circ}_{N}(y^{\star}):=\bigcap_{i}\left\{o_{1:H}:o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(140)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A6.E141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E141.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{F}^{\square}_{N}(y^{\star}):=\{o_{1:H}:\#\{i:o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\}\geq 1/2+\gamma_{N}/2\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}^{\square}_{N}(y^{\star}):=\{o_{1:H}:\#\{i:o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\}\geq 1/2+\gamma_{N}/2\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(141)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A6.E142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star}):=\mathcal{F}^{\circ}_{N}(y^{\star})\cap\mathcal{F}^{\square}_{N}(y^{\star})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star}):=\mathcal{F}^{\circ}_{N}(y^{\star})\cap\mathcal{F}^{\square}_{N}(y^{\star}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(142)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p7.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{definition}</span>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">[Inductive hypothesis for analysis]
Fix <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. For parameter <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{N,1},\delta_{N,2}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{N,1},\delta_{N,2}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{IH}_{N}(\delta_{N,1},\delta_{N,2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖨𝖧</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{IH}_{N}(\delta_{N,1},\delta_{N,2})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the following hypothesis. There are sets <math id="A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})\subseteq\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})\subseteq\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}</annotation></semantics></math> with the following properties:</p>
<ul id="A6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.E143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\delta_{N,1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\delta_{N,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(143)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-particle particle filtering algorithm <span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.E144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E144.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})]\leq\delta_{N,2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Alg</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})]\leq\delta_{N,2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(144)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the probability is over outputs <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> of <span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> executed on instance <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.3.2 </span>Base Case for Analysis</h4>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.E145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\mathcal{F}_{1}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\exp\left(-\gamma_{1}^{2}\frac{\mathfrak{H}(1)-2}{16}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\mathcal{F}_{1}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\exp\left(-\gamma_{1}^{2}\frac{\mathfrak{H}(1)-2}{16}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(145)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, for any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-particle particle filtering algorithm <span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span>,</p>
<table id="A6.E146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E146.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(1)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{1}(y^{\star})]\leq\exp\left(-\gamma_{1}^{2}\frac{\mathfrak{H}(1)-2}{12}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Alg</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(1)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{1}(y^{\star})]\leq\exp\left(-\gamma_{1}^{2}\frac{\mathfrak{H}(1)-2}{12}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(146)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> is executed on instance <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>Let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent with <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[X_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}]=1/2+\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[X_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}]=1/2+\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows from a Chernoff bound that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\mathcal{F}_{1}(y^{\star});y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\mathcal{F}_{1}(y^{\star});y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E147.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}[\#\{1&lt;h&lt;H:X_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}\}&gt;(1/2+\gamma_{1}/2)H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}[\#\{1&lt;h&lt;H:X_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}\}&gt;(1/2+\gamma_{1}/2)H]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(147)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E148.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\exp(-\gamma_{1}^{2}(\mathfrak{H}(1)-2)/16)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\exp(-\gamma_{1}^{2}(\mathfrak{H}(1)-2)/16)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(148)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which proves the first claim of the lemma. Next, fix any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-particle particle filtering algorithm <span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span>. Sample <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(1)})</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0},\dots,\mathcal{S}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be the stochastic sequence of multisets obtained by executing <span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> on <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>o</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o</annotation></semantics></math> be the output of <span id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span>. Then <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}=\{o_{1:h}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}=\{o_{1:h}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq h\leq H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq h\leq H</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the law of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0:h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0:h}</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}_{0}(\cdot;y^{\star}),\dots,\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}_{h}(\cdot;y^{\star}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}_{0}(\cdot;y^{\star}),\dots,\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}_{h}(\cdot;y^{\star}))</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds from the definition of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle 1}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\mathcal{S}_{0:h},y^{\star}_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{S}_{0:h},y^{\star}_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;h&lt;H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;h&lt;H</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> conditioned on <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\mathcal{S}_{0:h-1},y^{\star}_{1:h-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{S}_{0:h-1},y^{\star}_{1:h-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, and so we have</p>
<table id="A6.E149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E149.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[o_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:h-1},y^{\star}_{1:h-1}]=\frac{1}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[o_{h}=y^{\star}_{h}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:h-1},y^{\star}_{1:h-1}]=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(149)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="A6.SS3.SSS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;h&lt;H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;h&lt;H</annotation></semantics></math>. The second claim of the lemma then follows from Azuma’s inequality.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.3.3 </span>Inductive Step for Analysis</h4>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{IH}_{N-1}(\delta_{N-1,1},\delta_{N-1,2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖨𝖧</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{IH}_{N-1}(\delta_{N-1,1},\delta_{N-1,2})</annotation></semantics></math> holds. Suppose <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}(N-1)\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}(N-1)\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\in\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.E150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\frac{\mathfrak{H}(N)}{\mathfrak{H}(N-1)}\delta_{N-1,1}-\exp\left(-\gamma_{N}^{2}\frac{\mathfrak{H}(N)}{16\cdot\mathfrak{H}(N-1)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\frac{\mathfrak{H}(N)}{\mathfrak{H}(N-1)}\delta_{N-1,1}-\exp\left(-\gamma_{N}^{2}\frac{\mathfrak{H}(N)}{16\cdot\mathfrak{H}(N-1)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(150)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>Set <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H:=\mathfrak{H}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H:=\mathfrak{H}(N)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\sim\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\sim\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for each <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the law of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is precisely <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(\cdot;y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(\cdot;y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E151"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}^{\circ}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∘</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}^{\circ}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(151)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E152.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\sum_{i}\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\sum_{i}\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(152)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E153.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\frac{H}{K}\left(1-\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1});y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\frac{H}{K}\left(1-\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1});y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(153)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\frac{H}{K}\delta_{N-1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>H</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\frac{H}{K}\delta_{N-1,1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(154)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\frac{\mathfrak{H}(N)}{\mathfrak{H}(N-1)}\delta_{N-1,1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\frac{\mathfrak{H}(N)}{\mathfrak{H}(N-1)}\delta_{N-1,1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(155)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Next, note that the random variables <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(o_{iK+1})_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(o_{iK+1})_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]=1/2+\gamma_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]=1/2+\gamma_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</p>
<table id="A6.E156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E156.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}^{\square}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\exp(-\gamma_{N}^{2}(H/K)/8)\geq 1-\exp(-\gamma_{N}^{2}(\mathfrak{H}(N)/\mathfrak{H}(N-1))/16" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}^{\square}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\exp(-\gamma_{N}^{2}(H/K)/8)\geq 1-\exp(-\gamma_{N}^{2}(\mathfrak{H}(N)/\mathfrak{H}(N-1))/16</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(156)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">by Hoeffding’s inequality, so long as <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}(N-1)\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}(N-1)\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. The lemma follows from the union bound.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{N-1,1},\delta_{N-1,2},\delta_{N,2}\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{N-1,1},\delta_{N-1,2},\delta_{N,2}\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{IH}_{N-1}(\delta_{N-1,1},\delta_{N-1,2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖨𝖧</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{IH}_{N-1}(\delta_{N-1,1},\delta_{N-1,2})</annotation></semantics></math> holds. Set <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H:=\mathfrak{H}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H:=\mathfrak{H}(N)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K:=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K:=\mathfrak{H}(N-1)+2</annotation></semantics></math>. If</p>
<table id="A6.E157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{N}&gt;4\delta_{N-1,2}+\sqrt{\frac{8K\log(2/\delta_{N,2})}{H}}+\frac{8K}{H}\log(4/\delta_{N,2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{N}&gt;4\delta_{N-1,2}+\sqrt{\frac{8K\log(2/\delta_{N,2})}{H}}+\frac{8K}{H}\log(4/\delta_{N,2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(157)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">then for any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-particle particle filtering algorithm <span id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.E158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E158.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})]\leq\delta_{N,2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Alg</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})]\leq\delta_{N,2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(158)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">where <span id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> is executed on instance <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>Consider the random process induced by sampling <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})</annotation></semantics></math> and executing <span id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> on <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\cdot;y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and condition on <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the event that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{iK+1}\neq y^{\prime}_{iK+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{iK+1}\neq y^{\prime}_{iK+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y,y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y,y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, define process <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(0,b)},\dots,\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(0,b)},\dots,\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,b)}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(0,b)}=\{\varnothing\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(0,b)}=\{\varnothing\}</annotation></semantics></math> and, for each <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime},b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime},b)}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of the first <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq N-1</annotation></semantics></math> elements of</p>
<table id="A6.E159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E159.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{y_{iK+2:h^{\prime}+iK+1}:y_{1:h^{\prime}+iK+1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h^{\prime}+iK+1}\land y_{iK+1}=b\land y_{iK+2:h^{\prime}+iK}\in\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime}-1,b)}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{iK+2:h^{\prime}+iK+1}:y_{1:h^{\prime}+iK+1}\in\mathcal{S}_{h^{\prime}+iK+1}\land y_{iK+1}=b\land y_{iK+2:h^{\prime}+iK}\in\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime}-1,b)}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(159)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">according to some arbitrary ordering of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{h^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{h^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(0,b)},\dots,\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(0,b)},\dots,\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,b)}</annotation></semantics></math> describes the execution of an <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-particle myopic particle filtering algorithm on <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(\cdot;y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}(\cdot;y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. To see why, we check the conditions of <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Myopic Particle Filtering Algorithms ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>. First, it holds almost surely that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime},b)}|\leq N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime},b)}|\leq N-1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Second, by construction, if <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m21" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:h^{\prime}}\in\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime},b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:h^{\prime}}\in\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime},b)}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{1:h^{\prime}-1}\in\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime}-1,b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1:h^{\prime}-1}\in\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime}-1,b)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Third, for any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq h\leq K-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq h\leq K-2</annotation></semantics></math>, the law of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{(0,b)},\dots,\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime},b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{(0,b)},\dots,\mathcal{T}^{(h^{\prime},b)}</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by the law of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m25" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{0:h^{\prime}+iK+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{0:h^{\prime}+iK+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which by definition of <span id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> is determined by <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m27" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}_{h}(\cdot;y^{\star}):h\leq h^{\prime}+iK+1)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}_{h}(\cdot;y^{\star}):h\leq h^{\prime}+iK+1)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which by definition of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m29" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}_{k}(\cdot;y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}):0\leq k\leq h^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.710em">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{\mu}^{{\scriptscriptstyle N-1}}_{k}(\cdot;y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}):0\leq k\leq h^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> (together with randomness independent of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p4.m30" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">It follows from the inductive hypothesis that</p>
<table id="A6.E160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E160.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[\exists y\in\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,b)}\cap\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})]\leq\delta_{N-1,2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[\exists y\in\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,b)}\cap\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})]\leq\delta_{N-1,2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(160)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">In the event <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds almost surely that</p>
<table id="A6.E161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E161.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{y_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}:y_{1:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}\}=\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,0)}\cup\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}:y_{1:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}\}=\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,0)}\cup\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(161)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Moreover, the output <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="o_{1:H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{1:H}</annotation></semantics></math> of <span id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">Alg</span> satisfies <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="o_{1:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{1:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely, so</p>
<table id="A6.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E162"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E162.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(162)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E163"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E163.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}[\exists y_{1:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}:y_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}[\exists y_{1:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}:y_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(163)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E164.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}[\overline{\mathcal{E}}^{i}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]+\mathbb{P}[\exists y\in\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,0)}\cup\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,1)}:y_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}[\overline{\mathcal{E}}^{i}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]+\mathbb{P}[\exists y\in\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,0)}\cup\mathcal{T}^{(K-2,1)}:y_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(164)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E165"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E165.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}[\overline{\mathcal{E}}^{i}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]+2\delta_{N-1,2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{P}[\overline{\mathcal{E}}^{i}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]+2\delta_{N-1,2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(165)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Next, observe that in the event <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{E}}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{E}}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{iK+1}=\text{mode}\{y_{iK+1}:y\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>mode</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{iK+1}=\text{mode}\{y_{iK+1}:y\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}_{iK+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}_{iK+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</p>
<table id="A6.E166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E166.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[\text{mode}\{y_{iK+1}:y\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}\}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]=\frac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext>mode</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[\text{mode}\{y_{iK+1}:y\in\mathcal{S}_{(i+1)K-1}\}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]=\frac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(166)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Thus, we have</p>
<table id="A6.E167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E167.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]\leq\frac{1}{2}+\mathbb{P}[\mathcal{E}^{i}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]\leq\frac{1}{2}+\mathbb{P}[\mathcal{E}^{i}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(167)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.6" class="ltx_p">It follows that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E168"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E168.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(168)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E169"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E169.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}+\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]+2\delta_{N-1,2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}+\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]+2\delta_{N-1,2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(169)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.7" class="ltx_p">Define random variables</p>
<table id="A6.E170" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E170.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{i}:=\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]-\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}:=\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]-\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(170)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.8" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0},\dots,W_{H/K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0},\dots,W_{H/K}</annotation></semantics></math> is a martingale difference sequence under filtration induced by <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\mathcal{S}_{0:iK})_{i=0}^{H/K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{S}_{0:iK})_{i=0}^{H/K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, so for any <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.E171" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E171.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\left[\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}W_{i}&gt;\sqrt{8(H/K)\log(1/\delta)}\right]\leq\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\left[\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}W_{i}&gt;\sqrt{8(H/K)\log(1/\delta)}\right]\leq\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(171)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.9" class="ltx_p">Thus, with probability at least <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E172.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(172)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E173"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}+2\delta_{N-1,2}+\sqrt{\frac{8K\log(1/\delta)}{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}+2\delta_{N-1,2}+\sqrt{\frac{8K\log(1/\delta)}{H}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(173)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E174.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(174)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.10" class="ltx_p">By Freedman’s inequality, it holds with probability at least <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E175"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E175.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{P}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})\mid{}\mathcal{S}_{0:iK}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(175)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E176.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})]+8\log(2/\delta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})]+8\log(2/\delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(176)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.11" class="ltx_p">We conclude that with probability at least <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E177.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(177)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}+2\delta_{N-1,2}+\sqrt{\frac{8K\log(1/\delta)}{H}}+\frac{8K}{H}\log(2/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}+2\delta_{N-1,2}+\sqrt{\frac{8K\log(1/\delta)}{H}}+\frac{8K}{H}\log(2/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(178)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E179"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E179.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{2K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\frac{2K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(179)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.12" class="ltx_p">Condition on this event. If we moreover have <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="o_{1:H}\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{1:H}\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have both</p>
<table id="A6.E180" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E180.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]\geq\frac{1}{2}+\frac{\gamma_{N}}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+1}=y^{\star}_{iK+1}]\geq\frac{1}{2}+\frac{\gamma_{N}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(180)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.13" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A6.E181" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E181.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})]=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{K}{H}\sum_{i=0}^{H/K-1}\mathbb{I}[o_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N-1}(y^{\star}_{iK+2:(i+1)K-1})]=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(181)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.14" class="ltx_p">But then</p>
<table id="A6.E182" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\gamma_{N}}{2}\leq 2\delta_{N-1,2}+\sqrt{\frac{8K\log(1/\delta)}{H}}+\frac{8K}{H}\log(2/\delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\gamma_{N}}{2}\leq 2\delta_{N-1,2}+\sqrt{\frac{8K\log(1/\delta)}{H}}+\frac{8K}{H}\log(2/\delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(182)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.15" class="ltx_p">Set <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta:=\delta_{N,2}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta:=\delta_{N,2}/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Then this bound contradicts the lemma assumption, so in fact <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="o_{1:H}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{1:H}\not\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely (under the preceding condition). It follows that <math id="A6.SS3.SSS3.p5.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}[o_{1:H}\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})]\leq 2\delta=\delta_{N,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}[o_{1:H}\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})]\leq 2\delta=\delta_{N,2}</annotation></semantics></math> as claimed.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.3.4 </span>Completing the Induction</h4>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix some <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}(n):=N^{4n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}(n):=N^{4n}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n}:=1/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n}:=1/N</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">It holds that</p>
<table id="A6.E183" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\exp(-\Omega(N^{2}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\exp(-\Omega(N^{2}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(183)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="A6.E184" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E184.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})]\leq 4\exp(-N)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Alg</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(N)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star})]\leq 4\exp(-N).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(184)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof. </span>We have from <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS2" title="F.3.2 Base Case for Analysis ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.2</span></a> and <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS3" title="F.3.3 Inductive Step for Analysis ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.3</span></a> that</p>
<table id="A6.E185" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E185.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\sum_{n=1}^{N}\frac{\mathfrak{H}(N)}{\mathfrak{H}(n-1)}\exp(-\gamma_{n}^{2}\cdot\Omega(\mathfrak{H}(n)/\mathfrak{H}(n-1)))\geq 1-N^{4N+1}\exp(-\Omega(N^{2}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">N</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{{\scriptscriptstyle N}}(\mathcal{F}_{N}(y^{\star});y^{\star})\geq 1-\sum_{n=1}^{N}\frac{\mathfrak{H}(N)}{\mathfrak{H}(n-1)}\exp(-\gamma_{n}^{2}\cdot\Omega(\mathfrak{H}(n)/\mathfrak{H}(n-1)))\geq 1-N^{4N+1}\exp(-\Omega(N^{2})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(185)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Next, observe that if we set <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{n,2}:=4\exp(-N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{n,2}:=4\exp(-N)</annotation></semantics></math> then the condition of <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS3" title="F.3.3 Inductive Step for Analysis ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.3</span></a> is satisfied for each <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, so long as <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds a sufficiently large constant. Thus, applying <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS3" title="F.3.3 Inductive Step for Analysis ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.3</span></a> together with induction on <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> (with <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS2" title="F.3.2 Base Case for Analysis ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.2</span></a> providing the guarantee for <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=1</annotation></semantics></math>) proves that</p>
<table id="A6.E186" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E186.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(n)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{n}(y^{\star})]\leq 4\exp(-N)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>𝔼</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Alg</mtext></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EE_{y^{\star}\sim\mathsf{Unif}(\mathcal{A}^{\mathfrak{H}(n)})}\mathbb{P}_{o\sim\texttt{Alg}}[o\in\mathcal{F}_{n}(y^{\star})]\leq 4\exp(-N)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(186)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">for each <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> as needed.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Specialized Setting and Formal Theorem Statement ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>. </span>
Immediate from <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS4" title="F.3.4 Completing the Induction ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Sections</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.4</span></a> and <a href="#A6.SS3.SSS1.Px3" title="Formal construction: recursive case (𝑁&gt;1) ‣ F.3.1 Intuition and Formal Construction ‣ F.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix F Proof of ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3.1</span></a>, together with the fact that the <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-particle construction has horizon <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=\mathfrak{H}(N)=N^{4N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=\mathfrak{H}(N)=N^{4N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence <math id="A6.SS3.SSS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq\log(H)/(4\log\log(H))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq\log(H)/(4\log\log(H))</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Additional Experimental Details</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide further details regarding our experimental setup.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Additional Evaluation Approaches</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we give additional context and motivation for our choice of the evaluation metric of logprob-discrepancy introduced in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Controlled Setting: Prompt-Switching Task ‣ 4 Experiments in Language Models ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">One approach to evaluate SMC, which has been used in prior work, is to use the fact that the value <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{W}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{W}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> computed in <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Simple Criteria for Success of SMC ‣ 3 Theoretical Analysis of Particle Filtering Methods ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> satisfies <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{W}_{H}]=Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{W}_{H}]=Z</annotation></semantics></math> and moreover the difference <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log Z-\mathbb{E}[\log\widehat{W}_{H}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log Z-\mathbb{E}[\log\widehat{W}_{H}]</annotation></semantics></math> is an upper bound on the KL divergence <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathsf{KL}}\left(\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\nu}_{H}]\,\|\,\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathsf{KL}}\left(\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\nu}_{H}]\,\|\,\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> between the output distribution of SMC, <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\nu}_{H}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\nu}_{H}]</annotation></semantics></math>, and the target distribution <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition 5 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2024)</a></cite>).<span id="footnote9" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">9</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            Further, in <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Useful Lemmas for SMC ‣ Appendix C Proofs for SMC ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> we show that the difference <math id="footnote9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{W}_{H}-Z|</annotation></semantics></math> upper bounds the <em id="footnote9.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">total variation distance</em> <math id="footnote9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖳𝖵</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathsf{TV}}\left(\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\nu}_{H}],\pi^{\star}_{H}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span> However, there are several pitfalls with this approach: first, this is only an <em id="A7.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">upper bound</em> and is not guaranteed to be tight; further, it only applies to SMC and so does not allow us to compare the performance of SMC to other baselines. Finally, even for the relatively simple setting in which we operate, the number <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> of particles is too small to get actual <em id="A7.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">distributional</em> closeness between <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\nu}_{H}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\nu}_{H}]</annotation></semantics></math> and the target <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> (for instance, the action-level coverage is too large).</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we aimed to use a weaker notion of distributional closeness that we can both (a) measure efficiently and (b) hope to have some bearing on the quality of samples produced by SMC. The <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>-logprob discrepancy certainly satisfies (a). Moreover, since its error is one-sided in nature (i.e., <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LPD}_{\mathcal{P}}(\nu,\nu)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LPD</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LPD}_{\mathcal{P}}(\nu,\nu)=0</annotation></semantics></math>) and it takes on a positive value in all of our experiments, we believe it is a good candidate in the context of the prompt switching task.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Details for <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Evaluating Dependence on PRM Accuracy ‣ 4 Experiments in Language Models ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the prompt switching task in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Evaluating Dependence on PRM Accuracy ‣ 4 Experiments in Language Models ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, the prompts <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{p}_{\texttt{ref}},\texttt{p}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">p</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">p</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{p}_{\texttt{ref}},\texttt{p}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> were all generated with GPT-5.2 (in particular, the <span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">gpt-5.2_2025-12-11</span> release).</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To estimate <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathsf{KL}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}^{(i)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathsf{KL}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}^{(i)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we write</p>
<table id="A7.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{KL}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}^{(i)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>𝖪𝖫</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathsf{KL}}\left(\pi^{\star}_{h}\,\|\,\widehat{\pi}_{h}^{(i)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a_{1:h}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h}}\left[\log\frac{\pi^{\star}_{h}(a_{1:h})}{\widehat{\pi}_{h}^{(i)}(a_{1:h})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a_{1:h}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h}}\left[\log\frac{\pi^{\star}_{h}(a_{1:h})}{\widehat{\pi}_{h}^{(i)}(a_{1:h})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E187"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E187.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a_{1:h}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h}}\left[(1-h/H)\cdot\alpha\cdot\log\frac{\pi^{\star}(a_{1:h})}{\pi^{(i)}(a_{1:h})}\right]+\log\widehat{Z}^{(i)}_{h}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a_{1:h}\sim\pi^{\star}_{h}}\left[(1-h/H)\cdot\alpha\cdot\log\frac{\pi^{\star}(a_{1:h})}{\pi^{(i)}(a_{1:h})}\right]+\log\widehat{Z}^{(i)}_{h},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(187)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A7.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E188"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E188.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{Z}^{(i)}_{h}:=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}^{(i)}(a_{1:h})]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi^{\star}}\left[\left(\frac{\pi^{(i)}_{h}(a_{1:h})}{\pi^{\star}_{h}(a_{1:h})}\right)^{(1-h/H)\cdot\alpha}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{Z}^{(i)}_{h}:=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{ref}}}[\widehat{V}^{(i)}(a_{1:h})]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi^{\star}}\left[\left(\frac{\pi^{(i)}_{h}(a_{1:h})}{\pi^{\star}_{h}(a_{1:h})}\right)^{(1-h/H)\cdot\alpha}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(188)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We estimate the first term in <a href="#A7.E187" title="In G.2 Details for ‣ Appendix G Additional Experimental Details ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">187</span></a> via Monte Carlo rollouts from <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and estimate <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\widehat{Z}^{(i)}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\widehat{Z}^{(i)}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> via Monte Carlo rollouts from <math id="A7.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, per <a href="#A7.E188" title="In G.2 Details for ‣ Appendix G Additional Experimental Details ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">188</span></a> (each with 1000 samples).</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that our estimate of of <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Z}_{h}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Z}_{h}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is likely very noisy, since there is no logarithm inside the expectation. When we repeated the experiments without adding (our estimate of) the term <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\widehat{Z}_{h}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\widehat{Z}_{h}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> at all in <a href="#A7.E187" title="In G.2 Details for ‣ Appendix G Additional Experimental Details ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">187</span></a>, we observed similar results. Thus, the noise in our estimate of <math id="A7.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Z}_{h}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Z}_{h}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> seems unlikely to have affected our conclusions.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Details for the figures</h5>

<div id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S1.F2.sf2" title="In Figure 2 ‣ 1.3 Empirical Contributions: Does the Theory Predict the Performance of SMC in LLMs? ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(b)</span></a>, we use the PRM defined in <a href="#S4.E9" title="In 4.2 Evaluating Dependence on PRM Accuracy ‣ 4 Experiments in Language Models ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> with <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the KL divergences are measured at step <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=32</annotation></semantics></math> (recall that <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=64</annotation></semantics></math>); we observed similar results with other values of <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. The experiments were run on 32GB NVIDIA V100 GPUs. The Pearson correlation coefficient for the points plotted in <a href="#S1.F2.sf2" title="In Figure 2 ‣ 1.3 Empirical Contributions: Does the Theory Predict the Performance of SMC in LLMs? ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(b)</span></a> is 0.81.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A7.F7" title="In G.4 SMC vs. Best-of-𝑁 on AIME ‣ Appendix G Additional Experimental Details ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we plot additional runs of the same experiment as in <a href="#S1.F2.sf2" title="In Figure 2 ‣ 1.3 Empirical Contributions: Does the Theory Predict the Performance of SMC in LLMs? ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(b)</span></a>, with 3 additional different choices of the dataset (i.e., different choices of <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{p}_{\texttt{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">p</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{p}_{\texttt{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{p}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">p</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{p}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>). Finally, in <a href="#A7.F8" title="In G.4 SMC vs. Best-of-𝑁 on AIME ‣ Appendix G Additional Experimental Details ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we repeat the same experiment for all 4 datasets but with <math id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Details for <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Evaluating Dependence on Action-level Coverage ‣ 4 Experiments in Language Models ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A7.F6" title="In G.4 SMC vs. Best-of-𝑁 on AIME ‣ Appendix G Additional Experimental Details ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we repeat the experiment in <a href="#S1.F2.sf1" title="In Figure 2 ‣ 1.3 Empirical Contributions: Does the Theory Predict the Performance of SMC in LLMs? ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(a)</span></a> with 4 additional choices for the dataset (i.e., choices of <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{p}_{\texttt{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">p</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{p}_{\texttt{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{p}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">p</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{p}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[k]</annotation></semantics></math>). The Pearson correlation coefficients <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> are shown in the subcaptions of each subfigure. The experiments were run on 32GB NVIDIA V100 GPUs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.4 </span>SMC vs. Best-of-<math id="A7.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> on AIME</h3>

<div id="A7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our experiments on math problems in <a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 SMC on Math Problem-solving Tasks ‣ 4 Experiments in Language Models ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>, we used Qwen2.5-1B-Instruct as the base model <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> and Qwen2.5-Math-PRM-7B as the PRM <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. For both SMC and Best-of-<math id="A7.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, we used <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=32</annotation></semantics></math> particles/samples. We sampled from the base model with temperature <math id="A7.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, and used systematic resampling in the implementation of SMC. We generated for a maximum of 3072 tokens for AIME and a maximum of 2048 tokens for Math500.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As opposed to implementing SMC with <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> being the space of tokens (as in our experiments on prompt switching), we took <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the space of <em id="A7.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">blocks</em> of some number <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> of tokens; doing so significantly improves the efficiency of SMC, as calls to the PRM are the main computational bottleneck. We set <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=64</annotation></semantics></math> for Math500 and <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=128</annotation></semantics></math> for AIME. Moreover, we observed that the reward model <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{V}(a_{1:h})</annotation></semantics></math> often gave unreliable answers when passed as input a partial completion <math id="A7.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{1:h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1:h}</annotation></semantics></math> which was truncated in the middle of a sentence or mathematical expression. Thus, we in fact truncated all blocks at the last instance of a delimiter character (e.g., new line, period).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A7.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.07887v1/figures/aime24-smc-vs-bon/scatter-diff-n-32-vs-bon-n-32.png" id="A7.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/466;" width="476" height="466" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A7.F5.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A7.F5.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">AIME 2024</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A7.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.07887v1/figures/aime25-smc-vs-bon/scatter-diff-n-32-vs-bon-n-32.png" id="A7.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/466;" width="476" height="466" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A7.F5.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A7.F5.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">AIME 2025</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A7.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A7.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance of SMC vs. Best-of-<math id="A7.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> on AIME problems (each point is a different problem). Similar to <a href="#S1.F1" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Reject, Resample, Repeat: Understanding Parallel Reasoning in Language Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the majority of points lie below the line <math id="A7.F5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=x</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that SMC improves performance over Best-of-<math id="A7.F5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> on most problems.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A7.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="A7.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.07887v1/x1.svg" id="A7.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/357;" width="476" height="357"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A7.F6.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><math id="A7.F6.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.83" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.83</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.83</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
